var code = "<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <div id=\"link-to-quiz\" class=\"btn-back\">назад</div>\r\n\r\n  <h1>DSR JS Bootcamp 2025: entrance test</h1>\r\n\r\n  <strong>12 вопросов за 1 час</strong>\r\n  <ol>\r\n    <li>Test results, whether you passed or not, will be delivered via email, so please make sure to double-check the email address you enter.</li>\r\n    <li>There are 12 tasks in the test, you can't switch between them during the test.</li>\r\n    <li>You are not allowed to switch tabs or leave the test page during the exam. If you do so, you will receive a warning. After two warnings, your test will be automatically closed, and you will not be able to continue.</li>\r\n    <li>There's no time limit for each task, but be sure to complete all the tasks within 1 hour. You can follow our recommendations regarding time-management during the test:\r\n      <ol>\r\n        <li>Questions 1-5 - Single choice questions. Question 6 - short answer question. We recommend spending 10 minutes on this part.</li>\r\n        <li>Questions 7-9 - open answer. This part can take 15-20 minutes.</li>\r\n        <li>Question 10 - coding task. It can take 15-20 minutes.</li>\r\n        <li>Questions 11-12 - open answer tasks.</li>\r\n      </ol>\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ol>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>Question 1/12</h3>\r\n\r\n  <p>Which of the following is not a requirement for a RESTful application?</p>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>layered system</li>\r\n    <li><strong>writetable</strong></li>\r\n    <li>uniform interface</li>\r\n    <li>cacheable</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>Question 2/12</h3>\r\n\r\n  <p>Which of the following is not a valid CSS display property value?</p>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>inline-block</li>\r\n    <li><strong>outline</strong></li>\r\n    <li>none</li>\r\n    <li>flex</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>Question 3/12</h3>\r\n\r\n  <p>What is class in JS?</p>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Classes in JS art implemented as classic object-oriented model</li>\r\n    <li>Class is an object, which clones itself when constructor is called</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Class is a specific function</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Class is another name for prototype in JS</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>Question 4/12</h3>\r\n\r\n  <p>Wich exception call is syntactically incorrect in JavaScript</p>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>throw \"Error\";</li>\r\n    <li><strong>throw 404;</strong></li>\r\n    <li>throw false;</li>\r\n    <li>All options are correct</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>Question 5/12</h3>\r\n\r\n  <p>Which of the following HTML tags does not exist?</p>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>abbr</li>\r\n    <li>q</li>\r\n    <li>wbr</li>\r\n    <li><strong>color</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>Question 6/12</h3>\r\n\r\n  <p>What are data types in JS?</p>\r\n<pre>number, string, boolean, null,\r\nundefined, bigint, symbol, object</pre>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>Question 7/12</h3>\r\n\r\n  <p>What are the ways to declare a variable in JavaScript? What is the difference between them? What are the advantages and disadvantages of each variable type? In which situations would you use each type?</p>\r\n<pre>\r\nvar, const, let are used to declart variables\r\n\r\nvar for variables with function scope\r\nit has global scope if declared outside a function\r\nvariables declared with var are hoisted to the top of their scope\r\ncan be redeclared with same scope\r\nchangeable\r\n\r\nlet, const for variables with block scope\r\ncannot be redeclared with same scope\r\nlet is changeable\r\nconst is constant, not changeable, must initializate with declaration\r\n</pre>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>Question 8/12</h3>\r\n\r\n  <p>What is output of this code?</p>\r\n<pre>\r\nvar obj = {x: 3};\r\nvar arr = [];\r\n\r\narr.push(obj);\r\narr[0] = {x: 2};\r\n\r\nconsole.log(obj.x);\r\n</pre>\r\n  <code>3</code>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>Question 9/12</h3>\r\n\r\n  <p>What will you get in console after calling this function? Explain your answer</p>\r\n<pre>\r\n(function() {\r\n  console.log(1);\r\n\r\n  setTimeout( function() { console.log(2) }, 1000);\r\n\r\n  new Promise( () => console.log(3) );\r\n\r\n  setTimeout( function() { console.log(4) }, 0);\r\n\r\n  console.log(5);\r\n})();\r\n</pre>\r\n<pre>\r\n1\r\n3\r\n5\r\n4\r\n2\r\nconsole.log and create promise are run sequently\r\nafter run asyncron code\r\n</pre>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>Question 10/12</h3>\r\n\r\n  <p>Implement a function sum(num1)(num2)...() which can be called endlessly. Example</p>\r\n  <code>console.log(sum(2)());       // 2</code>\r\n  <code>console.log(sum(2)(3)());    // 5</code>\r\n  <code>console.log(sum(2)(3)(4)()); // 9</code>\r\n<pre>\r\nfunction sum(num) {\r\n  let summa = num;\r\n\r\n  function result(next) {\r\n    if (next === undefined) {\r\n      return summa;\r\n    }\r\n    summa += next;\r\n    return result;\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  return result;\r\n}\r\n</pre>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>Question 11/12</h3>\r\n\r\n  <p>What is the output of this code and why?</p>\r\n  <code>const wasmCode = new Uint8Array(\r\n    [0,97,115,109,1,0,0,0,\r\n    1,10,0,1,96,1,127,1,\r\n    127,3,2,1,0,7,5,1,\r\n    3,102,111,111,0,0,10,13,\r\n    1,11,0,65,42,11,0]\r\n    );</code>\r\n  <code>const wasmModule = new WebAssembly.Module(wasmCode);</code>\r\n  <code>wasmInstance = new WebAssembly.Instance(wasmModule);</code>\r\n  <code>console.log(wasmInstance.exports.foo());</code>\r\n  <code>42</code>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>Question 12/12</h3>\r\n\r\n  <p>Suggest REST API scheme for the following task:</p>\r\n  <p>You have jedi entities in your database.</p>\r\n  <p>Each entity has id (number), name (string), sex (male/female), skill (number from 1 to 10).</p>\r\n  <p>Your API needs to be able to create new Jedi (requires two existing Jedi with different genders), update skill for existing Jedi, get list of all Jedi and remove Jedi</p>\r\n  <p>Describe resources and URL, HTTP methods, request and response data schemes, how successful and failed requests should look like.</p>\r\n<pre>\r\nbase url https://api.jedi.com/v1\r\ncreate jedi\r\nmethod POST endpoint / jedi\r\nrequest body\r\n{\"name\": \"luke\", \"sex\": \"male\", \"parent1_id\": 1, \"parent2_id\": 2}\r\nresponse success (201 created)\r\n</pre>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n";
// Exports
/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = (code);

