var code = "<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <div id=\"link-to-quiz\" class=\"btn-back\">назад</div>\r\n\r\n  <h1>[hh.ru] Английский язык</h1>\r\n\r\n  <strong>14 вопросов. Выполнил на 10 баллов из 14</strong>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>1. One football player was _______ from the game, because he was using steroids.</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>put away</strong></li>\r\n    <li>banned</li>\r\n    <li>ejected</li>\r\n    <li>said goodbye</li>\r\n    <li>fired</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>2. Tom is extremely _______ person, heloves when people praise him.</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>vain</li>\r\n    <li>embarrassed</li>\r\n    <li>shy</li>\r\n    <li>stubborn</li>\r\n    <li><strong>proud</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>3. Select the wors which is simillar in its meaning to the word \"performance\"</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>dance</li>\r\n    <li><strong>productivity</strong></li>\r\n    <li>oppotrunity</li>\r\n    <li>suggestion</li>\r\n    <li>research</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>4. By the way, how ______ countries are there in ________ world?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>much - a</li>\r\n    <li><strong>many - the</strong></li>\r\n    <li>much - no article</li>\r\n    <li>much - the</li>\r\n    <li>many - a</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>5. In 1723, a young man named Benjamin Franklin came to Philadelphia with no money but a lot of ambition. Over time, he became very important to his city and country. He worked as a printer and was smart in many areas. He started a public library and a famous group for smart people called American Philosophical Society.\r\n  <br>Franclin made Philadelphia better. He added lights and paved roads, and started a police team and a fire-fighting group. He also invented useful things, like a special stove and a rod to protect buildings from lightning. People around the world knew him for his work with electricity.\r\n  <br>Franklin was also key in America's early history. He helped write important American documents and became the first representative to France. He played a role in ending a big war. In his later years, he worked hard to end slavery.</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Franklin arrived in Philadelphia with a lot of money and little ambition</li>\r\n    <li><strong>He contributed to his city by starting a public library and improving public infrastructure</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Franklin's primary contribution was in the field of literature</li>\r\n    <li>He was known globally for his culinary skills</li>\r\n    <li>He played no significant role in America's politics or international relations</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <p>6. What do three hearts, eight limbs, and one massive brain equal? An octopus, is a being that can perform remarkable feats. Octopuses are incredibly smart. They've mastered several techniques to escape challenging situations, such as when they sense danger from a foe. As octopuses lack teeth or pointed talons to protect themselves, they conceal themselves at the bottom of the sea. Curious about how they manage that? Well, the octopus acts as a chameleon sinse it can modify its skin hue to resemble the sediment. This alteration occurs in under 60 seconds. Some octopuses prefer dwelling in shallower waters near stones and corals. Because octopuses lack bones, they can compress themselves into tiny gaps amidst the stones to evade foes.</p>\r\n  <p>Another tactic an octopus employs is ejecting ink, An octopus utilizes a segment of its anatomy termes a siphon to spurt ink into the liquid. The ink creates a mist that veils the octopus. It's akin to an illusionist performing a disappearance trick. If an octopus faces assault, it can even mimic a toxic marine serpent. It will submerge itself in sediment, leaving two limbs exposed. It will alter the hue of those limbs to resemble a serpent.</p>\r\n  <p>But if there's no moment to conceal? If an octopus faced danger, it can detach one of its limb. The limb will then shift hues and wringgle in the liquid to divert the foe while the octopus propels away to refuge. Fear not, though. The octopup's limb will regenerate. There exists one species of octopus thet possesses toxin for protection. The blue-ringed octopus is minuscule, it can nestle in the crease of your paim. Foes might assume its size deems the octopus an appetizing morsel, but they're wary. The blue-ringed octopus is lethally toxic and can and foes much grander than itself, econompassing people.</p>  \r\n  <h3>Based on the text, which of the following statements about octopuses is NOT true?  </h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>The blue-ringed octopus uses venom as a means of protection</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Octopuses can eject ink to create a cloud that hides them from danger</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Octopuses can change the color of their skin to biend in with their surroundings</li>\r\n    <li>All octopuses have sharp teeth and talons for defense</li>\r\n    <li>Some octopuses can mimic the appearance of a toxic marine snake to scare off predators</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>7. Аудирование (0:15). What drinks do they get?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>a tea and three orange juices</li>\r\n    <li><strong>a coffee and three orange juices</strong></li>\r\n    <li>a coffee, a tea, and two orange juices</li>\r\n    <li>a coffee and a tea</li>\r\n    <li>a coffee, an orange juice and two teas</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>8. Аудирование (0:25). Why doesn't the woman want anything to eat?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Because she's on diet</li>\r\n    <li>Because she's not hungry</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Because she doesn't feel well</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Because she's not fat enough</li>\r\n    <li>Because she ate a lot the day before</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>9. Аудирование (0:20). The girl's new boyfriend is...</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>tall and with long dark hair</li>\r\n    <li><strong>short with short dark hair</strong></li>\r\n    <li>tall with short dark hair</li>\r\n    <li>short with long dark hair</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>10. Аудирование (1:14). Why doesn't the man like the Volvo car?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>The color is bad</li>\r\n    <li>Because it's not safety</li>\r\n    <li><strong>It's quite expensive</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The boot is too small</li>\r\n    <li>It has been scratched</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>11. Аудирование (1:14). What car do the man and the woman decide to buy in the end?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Peugeot</li>\r\n    <li><strong>They can't decide</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Volvo</li>\r\n    <li>VW</li>\r\n    <li>Golf</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>12. Аудирование (1:49). Why didn't James celebrate his 25th birthday?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>He was too busy with his successful career</li>\r\n    <li><strong>He felt he hadn't achieved anything significant in life</strong></li>\r\n    <li>He was away in a different country</li>\r\n    <li>He was focused on getting married</li>\r\n    <li>He doesn't enjoj birthday celebrations</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>13. Аудирование (1:49). What does Uncle Jack advise James to do about his feelings of dissatisfaction?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Try to change what he doesn't like and communicate his issues</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Compare himself more to his father</li>\r\n    <li>Suppress his feelings and avoid discussing them</li>\r\n    <li>Immediately find a wife like he did</li>\r\n    <li>Ignore his problems and focus on work</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>14. Аудирование (1:49). How did Uncle Jack react when his best friend got married?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>He disconnected from his friend</li>\r\n    <li>He was indifferent and focused on his career</li>\r\n    <li>He advised his friend against marriage</li>\r\n    <li>He felt content with his own single life</li>\r\n    <li><strong>He decided he also needed to marry and began searching intensely</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n";
