var code = "<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <div id=\"link-to-quiz\" class=\"btn-back\">назад</div>\r\n\r\n  <h1>[St1] Chrome DevTools</h1>\r\n\r\n  <strong>50 вопросов. Выполнил на 94 баллов из 100</strong>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>1. How can developers persist messages across page loads in Chrome DevTools Console?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Using the 'Preserve Log' option</strong></li>\r\n    <li>By saving the Console output as a file</li>\r\n    <li>Automatically on page reload</li>\r\n    <li>Through browser settings</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>2. How can developers step through their JavaScript code using Chrome DevTools?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Through the Performance panel</li>\r\n    <li>Using the Network panel</li>\r\n    <li>Via the Sources panel</li>\r\n    <li><strong>By the Console panel commands</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Using automated AI-based code analysis</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>3. How can developers test JavaScript in real-time using Chrome DevTools?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Using the Network panel</li>\r\n    <li>With the Performance panel</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Via the Console as a REPL</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Through the Elements panel</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>4. How can developers use the 'Computed' pane in Chrome DevTools to resolve CSS conflicts?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>By editing CSS directly</li>\r\n    <li><strong>By viewing final applied styles and their sources</strong></li>\r\n    <li>By checking network requests</li>\r\n    <li>By running JavaScript snippets</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>5. How can developers utilize the Console for modifying the page's content?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>By editing HTML in the Elements panel</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Through JavaScript commands in the Console</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Using CSS in the Styles panel</li>\r\n    <li>Via network request modifications</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>6. How can the 'Block Request' feature in the Network panel be used during development?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>To test a page's behavior without specific resources</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To speed up the page load time</li>\r\n    <li>To modify requests sent by a page</li>\r\n    <li>To analyze the content of blocked requests</li>\r\n    <li>To prioritize certain network requests over others</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>7. How can you filter local storage items in Chrome DevTools?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Using the filter box</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Through a Console command</li>\r\n    <li>By sorting the table</li>\r\n    <li>Not possible to filter</li>\r\n    <li>Through an advanced query builder tool</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>8. How does Chrome DevTools assist in identifying CSS values that have no effect due to other properties?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>By highlighting them in red</li>\r\n    <li><strong>By displaying them in pale text with an info icon</strong></li>\r\n    <li>By crossing them out</li>\r\n    <li>By showing a warning icon</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>9. How does one create a new key-value pair in local storage?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Double-clicking on the table</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Through a guided wizard in the Application panel</li>\r\n    <li>Right-clicking on the table</li>\r\n    <li>It's not possible to create new pairs</li>\r\n    <li>Perform a secret handshake with the local storage table</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>10. How does setting a line-of-code breakpoint help in JavaScript debugging?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Logs errors to the console</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Pauses execution at a specified line</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Monitors network requests</li>\r\n    <li>Analyzes performance metrics</li>\r\n    <li>Automatically corrects the code at the breakpoint</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>11. How does setting up a Workspace in the Sources panel benefit developers?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Enables code version control</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Saves changes to file system</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Improves network performance</li>\r\n    <li>Automates testing</li>\r\n    <li>Automatically syncs code changes with a cloud service</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>12. How does the 'Evaluate triggers user activation' setting affect JavaScript execution in the Console?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Changes the JavaScript context</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Enables user interaction simulations</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Alters the execution of async functions</li>\r\n    <li>Affects how scripts are loaded</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>13. How does the 'Layer Borders' tool aid in performance debugging?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>By highlighting areas with CSS layout issues</li>\r\n    <li><strong>By showing borders and tiles of page layers</strong></li>\r\n    <li>By marking elements with JavaScript event listeners</li>\r\n    <li>By identifying slow network requests</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>14. How does the 'Paint Flashing' tool in Chrome DevTools help developers?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It's like a disco for webpages</li>\r\n    <li>To debug JavaScript execution</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Highlights areas of a webpage undergoing repainting</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To check responsive design</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>15. How does throttling network speed in the Network panel aid developers?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>By enhancing the network security</li>\r\n    <li><strong>By simulating slower network conditions</strong></li>\r\n    <li>By increasing the page load speed</li>\r\n    <li>By monitoring WebSocket connections</li>\r\n    <li>It helps optimize server response times</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>16. How frequently do Live Expressions in Chrome DevTools' Console update their values?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Every 500 milliseconds</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Every 250 milliseconds</strong></li>\r\n    <li>In real-time without delay</li>\r\n    <li>Every 1 second</li>\r\n    <li>Only on days that end in 'y'</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>17. How is local storage data viewed in Chrome DevTools?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Via the Network panel</li>\r\n    <li>Through the Console</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Using the Application panel</strong></li>\r\n    <li>In the Elements panel</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>18. How is the 'Console' drawer used in debugging within Chrome DevTools?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>For viewing network logs</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To evaluate JavaScript in the current scope</li>\r\n    <li>To change CSS styles</li>\r\n    <li>To inspect HTML elements</li>\r\n    <li>Serves as a cozy chat room for your code snippets</li>\r\n    <li>Automatically suggests fixes for detected issues</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>19. In Chrome DevTools, which function allows you to quickly reposition the viewport to view a DOM node not currently in sight?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Inspect Element</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Scroll into View</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Force Element State</li>\r\n    <li>Capture Node Screenshot</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>20. In what ways does the 'Filter' function in Chrome DevTools assist with CSS debugging?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Filters network requests</li>\r\n    <li>Highlights syntax errors</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Searches for specific CSS properties</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Shows only overridden properties</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>21. Is it possible to interact with local storage from the Console panel?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Yes, through JavaScript</strong></li>\r\n    <li>No, it's view-only</li>\r\n    <li>Yes, but limited to viewing</li>\r\n    <li>No, it requires special extensions</li>\r\n    <li>Only data deletion is permitted via the Console</li>\r\n    <li>You can give motivational speeches to your local storage via the Console</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>22. What are the key tools in Chrome DevTools for diagnosing rendering performance problems? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Paint Flashing</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Layout Shift Regions</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Layer Borders</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Frame Rendering Stats</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Core Web Vitals</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>23. What are the uses of the 'Frame Rendering Stats' tool in performance analysis for developers?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To view memory usage</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To monitor real-time frame rates</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To analyze network requests</li>\r\n    <li>To inspect DOM elements</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>24. What can you do in the Styles pane of Chrome DevTools?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Change JavaScript code</li>\r\n    <li>Edit HTML structure</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Modify CSS properties</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Monitor network requests</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>25. What can you do with local storage key-value pairs in the Application panel?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Only view</li>\r\n    <li>View and edit</li>\r\n    <li><strong>View, edit, and delete</strong></li>\r\n    <li>No interaction possible</li>\r\n    <li>Synchronize them across different browsers</li>\r\n    <li>Export them as a JSON file for backup</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>26. What does Chrome DevTools provide to manage shorthand and longhand CSS properties?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Automatic conversion between shorthand and longhand</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Drop-down lists in the Styles pane</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Separate tabs for each</li>\r\n    <li>Color-coded distinction</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>27. What does crossing out a CSS declaration in the Styles pane indicate in Chrome DevTools?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Invalid CSS property</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Overridden CSS property</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Inactive CSS property</li>\r\n    <li>Syntax error in CSS</li>\r\n    <li>The CSS is playing a game of tic-tac-toe</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>28. What does enabling the 'Hide Network' option in Chrome DevTools Console do?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Hides network activity logs</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Improves network performance</li>\r\n    <li>Filters out network-related JavaScript logs</li>\r\n    <li>Disables network panel</li>\r\n    <li>It tells the network to play hide and seek</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>29. What does the 'Autocomplete from history' feature do in Chrome DevTools Console?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Suggests previously run commands</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Completes JavaScript code automatically</li>\r\n    <li>Remembers console command history</li>\r\n    <li>Predicts future JavaScript expressions</li>\r\n    <li>It automatically repeats the last executed command</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>30. What does the Console's utility function `debug()` do in Chrome DevTools?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Logs debugging information</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Pauses code on a function call</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Monitors performance</li>\r\n    <li>Tracks network activity</li>\r\n    <li>It's the panic button when your code goes rogue.</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>31. What does the 'Scope' pane in the Sources panel of Chrome DevTools display?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>HTML DOM changes</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Local and global variables</strong></li>\r\n    <li>CSS style modifications</li>\r\n    <li>Network activity logs</li>\r\n    <li>Displays a hierarchy of function calls</li>\r\n    <li>Reveals the secret life of variables</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>32. What feature does Chrome DevTools offer to understand why a CSS property is inactive?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Tooltip on hover</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Detailed error message</li>\r\n    <li>Link to external documentation</li>\r\n    <li>Console warnings</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>33. What feature does the Sources panel provide for editing CSS and JavaScript?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Inline editing in the Editor pane</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Separate editing window</li>\r\n    <li>Editing via the Console panel</li>\r\n    <li>Using external editors only</li>\r\n    <li>Automatically styles your code in your favorite color scheme</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>34. What feature in Chrome DevTools allows you to edit a node's type in the DOM Tree?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Edit as HTML</li>\r\n    <li>Duplicate Node</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Edit Node Type</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Force Element State</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>35. What feature in Chrome DevTools lets you apply a CSS pseudostate to an element?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>The ':hov' button located in the Styles pane</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Console commands</li>\r\n    <li>Elements panel options</li>\r\n    <li>Network conditions</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>36. What feature of Chrome DevTools allows viewing of logged messages?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Gossip Panel</li>\r\n    <li>Sources Panel</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Console Panel</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Network Panel</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>37. What happens when a new line is needed while typing a Live Expression in Chrome DevTools' Console?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>The expression is automatically executed</li>\r\n    <li>A new Live Expression is created</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Use Shift + Enter to start a new line</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The Console clears the current expression</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>38. What is the function of the console.assert() command in Chrome DevTools?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>To log a message if an assertion is false</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To stop JavaScript execution</li>\r\n    <li>Works exactly the same as console.log()</li>\r\n    <li>To monitor network requests</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>39. What is the implication of using the 'Force state' feature in the Elements panel of Chrome DevTools?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Temporarily changes the page layout</li>\r\n    <li>Permanently modifies the HTML file</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Temporarily applies CSS pseudo-classes such as :hover or :focus</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Forces a JavaScript event on the node</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>40. What is the primary function of Live Expressions in Chrome DevTools' Console?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To debug JavaScript errors</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To monitor real-time JavaScript values</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To edit HTML content</li>\r\n    <li>To analyze network requests</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>41. What is the primary function of the Snippets feature in Chrome DevTools' Sources panel?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Debugging JavaScript</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Running scripts on any page</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Monitoring network activity</li>\r\n    <li>Inspecting DOM elements</li>\r\n    <li>Automatically generates code based on the user's behavior</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>42. What is the primary purpose of the Network panel in Chrome DevTools?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To monitor HTTP headers of a request</li>\r\n    <li>To inspect JavaScript source code</li>\r\n    <li>To modify CSS styles in real-time</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To track and analyze network activity of web pages</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To manage client-side caching mechanisms</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>43. What is the purpose of Event Listener Breakpoints in Chrome DevTools?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To debug JavaScript errors</li>\r\n    <li>To monitor network requests</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To pause code at specific DOM events</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To edit JavaScript in real-time</li>\r\n    <li>To log all events triggered on the page</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>44. What is the purpose of the Box Model in Chrome DevTools?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>For JavaScript debugging</li>\r\n    <li>To wrap virtual gifts for your favorite DOM elements</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To adjust and view an element's CSS Box Model properties</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To inspect the DOM hierarchy</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>45. What is the purpose of the 'Core Web Vitals' overlay in Chrome DevTools?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To measure JavaScript execution time</li>\r\n    <li>To identify page layout instability</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To provide insights on user-centric performance metrics</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To optimize CSS rendering</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>46. What is the purpose of the 'element.style' section in the Styles pane?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To view the computed style</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To add inline CSS to an element</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To edit the external CSS file</li>\r\n    <li>To inspect JavaScript bound to the element</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>47. What is the significance of 'Focus only on your code' in the Sources panel?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Filtering out third-party code</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Highlighting syntax errors</li>\r\n    <li>Enhancing code readability</li>\r\n    <li>Optimizing performance</li>\r\n    <li>Turns the Sources panel into a no-distraction zen garden</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>48. What method in Chrome DevTools is used to add a new CSS class to an element?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Using the .cls option in the Styles pane</strong></li>\r\n    <li>By editing the HTML directly</li>\r\n    <li>Via the Console panel</li>\r\n    <li>Through the Elements panel context menu</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>49. What shortcut key combination opens the Command menu in Chrome DevTools for enabling rulers on hover? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Control + Shift + P</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Alt + Shift + P</li>\r\n    <li>Control + Alt + P</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Command + Shift + P (Mac)</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Alt + F4</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>50. What type of network activity can be captured using the 'Capture Screenshots' feature in the Network panel?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Changes in CSS styles over time</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Screenshots of how a page looked during loading</strong></li>\r\n    <li>JavaScript errors occurring during page load</li>\r\n    <li>HTML DOM mutations during page load</li>\r\n    <li>Capturing user interactions during network calls</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n";
// Exports
/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = (code);

