var code = "<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <div id=\"link-to-quiz\" class=\"btn-back\">назад</div>\r\n\r\n  <h1>[St1] Client - Server interaction</h1>\r\n\r\n  <strong>33 вопроса. Выполнил на 94 баллов из 100</strong>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>1. Choose the correct statements about AES and RSA. (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>AES is an encoding scheme</li>\r\n    <li>RSA is a hashing algorithm</li>\r\n    <li><strong>AES is a symmetric encryption algorithm</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>RSA is an asymmetric encryption algorithm</strong></li>\r\n    <li>They are ancient martial arts forms</li>\r\n    <li>RSA uses the same key for encryption and decryption</li>\r\n    <li>RSA is the 'Royal Society of Aliens' favorite encryption method</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>2. How does a client-server model work in the context of the web?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>The client provides data storage</li>\r\n    <li>The server makes requests to the client</li>\r\n    <li>Both client and server perform the same roles</li>\r\n    <li><strong>The client requests resources, and the server provides them</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>3. In HTTP, what does 'persistent connection' mean?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>A connection that survives even a zombie apocalypse</li>\r\n    <li><strong>A connection that remains open for further requests after the first one</strong></li>\r\n    <li>A connection that automatically reopens if it's closed</li>\r\n    <li>A connection that uses persistent cookies</li>\r\n    <li>A connection that cannot be closed</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>4. In HTTP, what does the term 'stateless' imply?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Servers have amnesia after each request</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The protocol does not maintain any state between different message exchanges</li>\r\n    <li>All HTTP requests must be sent in a single batch</li>\r\n    <li>The server undergoes frequent state changes</li>\r\n    <li>The server retains user data between different requests</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>5. In HTTP, what is the purpose of a 'Cache-Control' header?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To control user access to the cached content</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To specify caching policies for the document being sent</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To compress the data in the cache</li>\r\n    <li>To monitor cache sizes on the client</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>6. In SSL, what role does a Certificate Authority (CA) play?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It speeds up the encryption process</li>\r\n    <li>It designs the website's layout</li>\r\n    <li><strong>It issues digital certificates</strong></li>\r\n    <li>It monitors website traffic</li>\r\n    <li>It maintains a list of expired certificates</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>7. In the OSI Model, which layer encapsulates data for transmission between networks?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Transport Layer</li>\r\n    <li>Session Layer</li>\r\n    <li>Application Layer</li>\r\n    <li>Network Layer</li>\r\n    <li>Envelope Layer</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Data Link Layer</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>8. The Application Layer of the OSI Model is not responsible for:</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Routing data</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Network resource access</li>\r\n    <li>User interface provision</li>\r\n    <li>Providing network services</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>9. What are common methods to ensure SSL implementation on a website? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Installing an SSL certificate</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Regularly updating website content</li>\r\n    <li>Redirecting HTTP to HTTPS</li>\r\n    <li>Using strong passwords</li>\r\n    <li>Performing digital rain dances</li>\r\n    <li>Conducting periodic security audits</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>10. What does 'HTTPS' stand for?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>HyperText Transfer Protocol Secure</strong></li>\r\n    <li>HyperText Transfer Protocol for Superheroes</li>\r\n    <li>HyperText Transmission Protocol Secure</li>\r\n    <li>HyperText Transfer Protocol Suite</li>\r\n    <li>HyperText Transfer Protocol Speed</li>\r\n    <li>HyperText Transmission Protocol Safety</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>11. What does the Physical Layer in the OSI Model primarily focus on?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Routing protocols</li>\r\n    <li>Data encryption</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Physical transmission of data</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Session management</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>12. What is a 'cookie' in web browsing?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>A sweet snack</li>\r\n    <li>A tool for hacking websites</li>\r\n    <li><strong>A small piece of data stored on the user's computer</strong></li>\r\n    <li>A device to speed up the internet</li>\r\n    <li>A method for maintaining session state</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>13. What is a fundamental feature of Base64 encoding?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It uses a key for encoding and decoding</li>\r\n    <li>It compresses data into binary format</li>\r\n    <li>It is an encryption algorithm</li>\r\n    <li><strong>It translates binary data into ASCII format</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>14. What is a key distinction of asymmetric encryption?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It is mainly used for data compression</li>\r\n    <li>It uses identical keys for encryption and decryption</li>\r\n    <li><strong>It uses two different keys – a public key and a private key</strong></li>\r\n    <li>It is faster than symmetric encryption</li>\r\n    <li>It involves a secret handshake between keys</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>15. What is a key feature of symmetric encryption?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Uses a different key for encryption and decryption</li>\r\n    <li>Is primarily used for hashing</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Uses the same key for encryption and decryption</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Operates only on text data</li>\r\n    <li>Involves a secret handshake</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>16. What is CORS primarily used for in web development?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To encrypt data sent over HTTP</li>\r\n    <li>To style web pages</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To allow a server to indicate which origins can load its resources</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To speed up website performance</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>17. What is the main function of a Domain Name System (DNS)?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To encrypt internet traffic</li>\r\n    <li>To store website content</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To translate domain names into IP addresses</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To speed up internet connection</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>18. What is the main function of a 'User-Agent' string in HTTP?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To authenticate the user's identity</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To identify the browser and operating system to the server</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To encrypt data between the client and server</li>\r\n    <li>To measure the internet speed of the user</li>\r\n    <li>To help in mobile device detection and optimization</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>19. What is the main purpose of encryption?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To speed up data transmission</li>\r\n    <li>To compress data files</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To convert data into a secure format to prevent unauthorized access</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To create a backup of the data</li>\r\n    <li>To make data readable by aliens</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>20. What is the main reason for the CORS preflight request?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To check server availability</li>\r\n    <li>To ask the server, \"Are you ready for this?\"</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To check that the server will permit the actual request</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To authenticate the user</li>\r\n    <li>To retrieve data before the actual request</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>21. What is the primary purpose of an IP address in the context of the internet?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To identify a user's location</li>\r\n    <li>To encrypt data</li>\r\n    <li>To increase internet speed</li>\r\n    <li>To facilitate network communication</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To provide a unique identifier for each device</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>22. What is the primary purpose of HTTP?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To encrypt data sent over the internet</li>\r\n    <li>To compress data to reduce transmission time</li>\r\n    <li>To generate and manage website cookies</li>\r\n    <li>To define the structure of messages between web servers and browsers</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To provide a protocol for transferring data over the web</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>23. What is the primary purpose of SSL?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To speed up website performance</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To encrypt communications between a web server and a browser</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To provide a graphical interface for websites</li>\r\n    <li>To increase website storage capacity</li>\r\n    <li>To serve as a digital doorman for websites</li>\r\n    <li>To ensure data integrity in web transactions</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>24. What is the primary purpose of the OSI Model?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>To provide a standardized framework for network design</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To increase internet speed</li>\r\n    <li>To encrypt network communications</li>\r\n    <li>To monitor network performance</li>\r\n    <li>To define layers for troubleshooting network issues</li>\r\n    <li>To predict the future of internet trends</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>25. What is the role of the Session Layer in the OSI Model?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Data encryption</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Managing communication sessions</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Physical data transmission</li>\r\n    <li>Data format conversion</li>\r\n    <li>Coordinating communication between devices</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>26. What status code class does '404 Not Found' belong to in HTTP?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>0xx Existential crises</li>\r\n    <li>2xx Success</li>\r\n    <li><strong>4xx Client errors</strong></li>\r\n    <li>5xx Server errors</li>\r\n    <li>3xx Redirection</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>27. Which HTTP method is typically used to request the contents of a web page?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>POST</li>\r\n    <li><strong>GET</strong></li>\r\n    <li>CONNECT</li>\r\n    <li>TRACE</li>\r\n    <li>ASK POLITELY</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>28. Which language is predominantly used for client-side scripting to make web pages interactive?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Python</li>\r\n    <li>C++</li>\r\n    <li>HTML</li>\r\n    <li><strong>JavaScript</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Elvish</li>\r\n    <li>TypeScript</li>\r\n    <li>ECMAScript</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>29. Which layer of the OSI Model is responsible for data format standardization?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Session Layer</li>\r\n    <li>Network Layer</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Presentation Layer</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Fashion Layer</li>\r\n    <li>Data Link Layer</li>\r\n    <li>Physical Layer</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>30. Which layer of the OSI Model is responsible for reliable data transfer between end systems?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Teleportation Layer</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Transport Layer</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Application Layer</li>\r\n    <li>Presentation Layer</li>\r\n    <li>Data Link Layer</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>31. Which of the following is a characteristic of TCP in the context of internet communication?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Transmission of data without establishing a connection</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Guarantees delivery of packets in the order sent</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Only used for email communication</li>\r\n    <li>Does not require an IP address</li>\r\n    <li>Transmits Cat Pictures</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>32. Which of the following is a security measure enforced by browsers in relation to CORS?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Encrypting all scripts</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Restricting cross-origin HTTP requests initiated from scripts</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Disabling JavaScript</li>\r\n    <li>Automatically deleting cookies</li>\r\n    <li>Sending a virtual security guard</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>33. Which of the following methods are idempotent in HTTP? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>POST</li>\r\n    <li><strong>GET</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>PUT</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>DELETE</strong></li>\r\n    <li>YELL</li>\r\n    <li><strong>OPTIONS</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>34. Which OSI layer handles error detection and correction? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Transport Layer</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Network Layer</li>\r\n    <li>Physical Layer</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Data Link Layer</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Comedy Layer</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>35. Which protocol does SSL directly enhance the security of?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>HTTP</strong></li>\r\n    <li>FTP</li>\r\n    <li>SMTP</li>\r\n    <li>UDP</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>36. Which protocol is primarily used for secure communication over the internet?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>UFO (Unidentified Flying Object Protocol)</li>\r\n    <li>SMTP (Simple Mail Transfer Protocol)</li>\r\n    <li>HTTP (Hypertext Transfer Protocol)</li>\r\n    <li>TLS (Transport Layer Security)</li>\r\n    <li>FTP (File Transfer Protocol)</li>\r\n    <li><strong>HTTPS (Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure)</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n";
// Exports
/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = (code);

