var code = "<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <div id=\"link-to-quiz\" class=\"btn-back\">назад</div>\r\n\r\n  <h1>[St2] Code-Review</h1>\r\n\r\n  <strong>33 вопроса. Выполнил на 82 баллов из 100</strong>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>1. How can a code author improve the code review process? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Providing clear and concise descriptions</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Automating as much as possible</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Skipping unnecessary reviews</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Submitting large changes for review</strong></li>\r\n    <li>By not running any tests</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>2. How can code reviewers reduce context switching?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>By reviewing all code at the end of the day</li>\r\n    <li>By ignoring code reviews</li>\r\n    <li>By multitasking more efficiently</li>\r\n    <li>By using a magic crystal ball to predict code issues</li>\r\n    <li><strong>By scheduling dedicated times for code reviews</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>3. How can review requests be managed in a GitHub pull request?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Through automated suggestions based on code analysis</li>\r\n    <li>Asking a magic 8-ball for advice</li>\r\n    <li>Using carrier pigeons</li>\r\n    <li><strong>By adding users to your pull request for feedback</strong></li>\r\n    <li>By sending a formal invitation letter</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>4. How do code reviews help in spreading product knowledge?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Focusing exclusively on external documentation for knowledge transfer</li>\r\n    <li>By restricting knowledge to senior members</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Enabling exposure to various aspects of the codebase, enhancing overall understanding</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Limiting knowledge sharing to formal, structured training sessions</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>5. How does GitHub's 'Blame' feature assist developers?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To play practical jokes on team members</li>\r\n    <li>By revealing who ate the last slice of pizza</li>\r\n    <li><strong>It assigns blame to developers for broken code</strong></li>\r\n    <li>By showing how a file looked before a specific change</li>\r\n    <li>It helps in identifying the most productive developer</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>6. How should complexity be assessed in a code review?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>If the code can be understood quickly</strong></li>\r\n    <li>By the number of coffee breaks taken during coding</li>\r\n    <li>By the weight of the computer running the code</li>\r\n    <li>The age of the developer</li>\r\n    <li>The color of the code in the editor</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>7. How should reviewers approach understanding the context of a code change?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Only focusing on the code, not the context</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Relying on the code change description</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Ignoring the context completely</li>\r\n    <li>By guessing the author's intent</li>\r\n    <li>Asking the author to explain it in person</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>8. In a code review, what is an important aspect of the review feedback?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Providing feedback in a cryptic manner</li>\r\n    <li>Ignoring minor issues</li>\r\n    <li>Only pointing out major bugs</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Being constructive and empathetic</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Rating each line of code with an emoji for expressiveness</li>\r\n    <li>Focusing only on syntax errors</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>9. What are the benefits of involving junior developers in code reviews?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>For training and learning purposes</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Because they bring snacks to the review meetings</li>\r\n    <li>To increase the number of reviewers</li>\r\n    <li>To make coffee for senior developers</li>\r\n    <li>Junior developers are always right</li>\r\n    <li>For entertainment value</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>10. What are the benefits of small, incremental code changes in reviews? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Makes the code look mysterious</li>\r\n    <li>Less intimidating for new reviewers</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Enhances bug detection probability</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Reduces the complexity of reviews</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Better for tracking changes</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Easier to understand for reviewers</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>11. What can be used on GitHub to maintain the integrity of your code?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Shouting motivational quotes at the screen</li>\r\n    <li>Duct tape</li>\r\n    <li>A secret handshake</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Protected branches</strong></li>\r\n    <li>A magic spell</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>12. What can you do with GitHub's pull request timeline interface?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Organize your vacation photos</li>\r\n    <li>Predict future code changes</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Browse commits, comments, and references related to a pull request</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Check the weather forecast</li>\r\n    <li>Time travel to the date of the first commit</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>13. What do GitHub's 'Permissions' in code review allow?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Setting visibility levels for different parts of the repository</li>\r\n    <li>To restrict internet access</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To control who can push to a branch</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To grant access to secret company recipes</li>\r\n    <li>Determining who gets the last donut</li>\r\n    <li>To decide who gets the corner office</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>14. What does a wide net of reviewers in code reviews ensure?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Initiating a debate club atmosphere among the developers</li>\r\n    <li>Introducing increased bureaucratic layers in the review procedure</li>\r\n    <li>Reducing reliance on automated testing tools</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Ensuring comprehensive coverage and decentralizing the review process</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Allowing only popular developers to have their code reviewed</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>15. What does GitHub allow you to resolve directly on the platform?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Deciding what to eat for lunch</li>\r\n    <li>Disputes between team members</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Simple merge conflicts</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Internet connectivity issues</li>\r\n    <li>Existential crises</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>16. What does peer review in code reviews encourage?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Sole reliance on automated testing, bypassing human review</li>\r\n    <li>Prioritizing individual effort over collaborative team work</li>\r\n    <li>Coding in a secretive manner to avoid peer review</li>\r\n    <li>Competitiveness among developers</li>\r\n    <li>Writing elaborate fictional comments in code to entertain reviewers.</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Writing high-quality code with the awareness that it will undergo scrutiny</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>17. What does reviewing every line of code ensure?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>The code has a nice rhythm</li>\r\n    <li>It ensures reviewers get no sleep</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Understanding of what all the code is doing</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The code forms a secret message</li>\r\n    <li>That reviewers feel overwhelmed</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>18. What does the side-by-side 'Diffs' feature on GitHub highlight?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Alien messages hidden in the code</li>\r\n    <li>Code performance metrics</li>\r\n    <li>The best coding practices</li>\r\n    <li>The developer's coding style preferences</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Added, edited, and deleted code next to the original file</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>19. What is a crucial element of code reviews in the context of mentoring new engineers?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Assigning the review of complex code segments exclusively to new engineers</li>\r\n    <li>Assigning code names to new engineers and communicating in Morse code</li>\r\n    <li>Limiting new engineers to simplistic tasks to avoid complexity</li>\r\n    <li>Actively discouraging inquiries from new engineers to toughen them up</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Facilitating discussions and sharing knowledge about the code base</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Experienced engineers critiquing without providing constructive feedback</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>20. What is a key benefit of adding experienced reviewers in a code review?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To make junior developers feel inexperienced</li>\r\n    <li>They take less time to review</li>\r\n    <li>They use their psychic powers to find bugs</li>\r\n    <li>Experienced reviewers never make mistakes</li>\r\n    <li>Experienced reviewers use their telekinetic powers to fix code on the fly</li>\r\n    <li><strong>They tend to give more insightful feedback</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>21. What is a key benefit of code reviews for agile teams? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Improving estimation accuracy</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Sharing knowledge across the team</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Restricting code writing to senior developers only</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Reducing the need for project management</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Preventing the participation of new developers</li>\r\n    <li>Discovering the finest local coffee establishments</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>22. What is a key consideration for comments in code?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Comments should be cryptic and mysterious</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Comments should explain why some code exists</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Comments should use Shakespearean English</li>\r\n    <li>Comments should be in haiku form</li>\r\n    <li>Comments should narrate a fantasy story</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>23. What is a key element in the success of a code review?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>The number of coffee breaks taken</li>\r\n    <li>Focusing solely on finding bugs</li>\r\n    <li>Using the most expensive code editor</li>\r\n    <li><strong>The communication quality between author and reviewers</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Using a specific programming language</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>24. What is a recommended practice for code authors when submitting a code review?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To submit without any description</li>\r\n    <li>To only use emojis in the description</li>\r\n    <li>To expect reviewers to understand without a description</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To include a detailed description of the changes</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To wait for reviewers to ask questions</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>25. What is crucial to check about tests in a code review?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Whether tests are correct and useful</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The number of test files</li>\r\n    <li>The color of the test output</li>\r\n    <li>If the tests can predict the weather</li>\r\n    <li>If the tests have nice names</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>26. What is essential to review in terms of documentation? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>If the documentation is written in iambic pentameter</li>\r\n    <li>Whether documentation includes fun facts</li>\r\n    <li><strong>If documentation reflects changes in how users interact with the app</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Whether documentation is updated with code changes</strong></li>\r\n    <li>If the documentation includes a cookie recipe</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>27. What is important about naming in code?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Names should be as long as possible</li>\r\n    <li>Names should reflect the developer's pets</li>\r\n    <li>Names should be humorous</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Names should fully communicate what the item is or does</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Names should be in Latin</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>28. What is the primary aspect to consider in a code review?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>The time of day the code was written</li>\r\n    <li>The font size used in the code</li>\r\n    <li>The color scheme of the code editor</li>\r\n    <li>The developer's coding speed</li>\r\n    <li><strong>The overall design of the code</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>29. What is the primary function of GitHub's 'Comments' feature in code reviews?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>To leave detailed comments on code syntax and structure</strong></li>\r\n    <li>For posting memes</li>\r\n    <li>For documenting bug reports and tracking issues</li>\r\n    <li>Commenting on the latest fashion trends</li>\r\n    <li>To rate developers' performance</li>\r\n    <li>For casual chatting</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>30. What is the primary purpose of a code review in agile development?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To identify logical errors and confirm compliance with all requirements</li>\r\n    <li>To reduce the number of comments in the code</li>\r\n    <li>To verify the code compiles without any errors</li>\r\n    <li>To play a prank on the intern</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To optimize the runtime efficiency of the code</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>31. What is the purpose of 'Required status checks' on GitHub?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To verify if coffee is available in the office</li>\r\n    <li>To check the status of the server</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To ensure only high-quality code gets merged</strong></li>\r\n    <li>For checking the weather status</li>\r\n    <li>To monitor the stock market</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>32. What is the role of consistency in code review?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Code should be consistently cryptic</li>\r\n    <li>Consistency refers to the mood of the developer</li>\r\n    <li>Consistency ensures the code has a consistent color theme</li>\r\n    <li>Code should consistently include jokes</li>\r\n    <li><strong>New code should be consistent with style guidelines or existing code</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>33. What role does automation play in code reviews?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It replaces manual reviews completely</li>\r\n    <li><strong>It helps catch syntax errors and enforce style guides</strong></li>\r\n    <li>It's not used in code reviews</li>\r\n    <li>Only for generating funny comments</li>\r\n    <li>Automation writes the code itself</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>34. What should be avoided when selecting reviewers for your code change?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Selecting too many reviewers</li>\r\n    <li>Adding inexperienced reviewers</li>\r\n    <li>Asking for external reviewers</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Choosing reviewers from the same team</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>35. What should be ensured about code style in a review?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Code style reflects the latest fashion trends</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Code follows the appropriate style guides</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Code is stylish and trendy</li>\r\n    <li>Style should match the reviewer's personal preference</li>\r\n    <li>Code style changes with each season</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>36. What should code reviewers focus on regarding functionality?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Whether the code can make coffee</li>\r\n    <li>The number of lines in the code</li>\r\n    <li>The brand of the developer's computer</li>\r\n    <li><strong>If the code does what the developer intended</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The programming language used</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>37. When should a code review be initiated in an agile team?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Whenever the office cat wanders into the room</li>\r\n    <li>Following the merge of code into the main branch</li>\r\n    <li><strong>After code is written and tests are passed, but before merging into the main branch</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Once a year during performance reviews</li>\r\n    <li>At the end of each sprint</li>\r\n    <li>Prior to commencing any code development</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>38. Why are code reviews important before merging code?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Creating an additional layer of documentation requirements</li>\r\n    <li>Prolonging the code review process unnecessarily</li>\r\n    <li>Conducting a ritual to appease the coding gods for smooth functionality</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To catch any poor decisions or errors before they affect the main codebase</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To ensure that only the team leader's code is merged</li>\r\n    <li>Using the review process as a strategy to procrastinate on deadlines</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>39. Why is it important to give timely feedback in code reviews?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It's not important; delays are expected</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To prevent blocking the code author</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Feedback is not time-sensitive</li>\r\n    <li>To showcase rapid response skills</li>\r\n    <li>It helps in winning a speed contest</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>40. Why is running tests before submitting a code review important?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It ensures code reviewers have more work</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To ensure the code works as expected</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To show off the latest test animations</li>\r\n    <li>It's a way to demonstrate programming skills</li>\r\n    <li>Tests are not important in code reviews</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n";
// Exports
/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = (code);

