// Module
var code = "<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <div id=\"link-to-quiz\" class=\"btn-back\">назад</div>\r\n\r\n  <h1>Test CSS Basics</h1>\r\n\r\n  <strong>33 вопроса. Выполнил на 100 баллов из 100</strong>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>1. According to the documentation (to MDN), where should the style tag be placed? (The W3C validator will not throw an error)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>outside the html tag</li>\r\n    <li>in the html tag but not in the head or body</li>\r\n    <li><strong>in the head tag</strong></li>\r\n    <li>in the body tag</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>2. At what value of the text-align property will the text be aligned to the right?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>right</strong></li>\r\n    <li>center</li>\r\n    <li>left</li>\r\n    <li>justify</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>3. By default, an element with {position: absolute} (without any other positioning properties) will be aligned to which edge of its nearest positioned ancestor?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>top right</li>\r\n    <li>bottom right</li>\r\n    <li>bottom left</li>\r\n    <li><strong>top left</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>4. Does Cascading allow you to combine styles from different sources?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>yes</strong></li>\r\n    <li>no</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>5. For the Mozilla Firefox browser, the vendor prefix for styles looks like this:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>-ms-</li>\r\n    <li>-webkit-</li>\r\n    <li><strong>-moz-</strong></li>\r\n    <li>-ff-</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>6. How do you make an element's content and its children unselectable using CSS?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>content: none;</li>\r\n    <li>pointer-events: none;</li>\r\n    <li><strong>user-select: none;</strong></li>\r\n    <li>child-select: none;</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>7. If the parent element is given a font size of 24px, then this size will be inherited:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>nested elements of the first level only</li>\r\n    <li><strong>all nested elements</strong></li>\r\n    <li>no nested element will inherit size</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>8. If the variable is written as :root {--main-color: #000;}, then you can apply it like this:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>color: parse(--main-color);</li>\r\n    <li><strong>color: var(--main-color);</strong></li>\r\n    <li>color: root(--main-color);</li>\r\n    <li>color: --main-color;</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>9. In a multiline text element, line spacing can be changed using the property:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>line-height</strong></li>\r\n    <li>height</li>\r\n    <li>padding</li>\r\n    <li>padding-bottom</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>10. In order to set the style directly in the element (write the style inline), use the attribute:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>style</strong></li>\r\n    <li>css</li>\r\n    <li>stylesheet</li>\r\n    <li>text</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>10. In the entry {font: bold italic, 24 px Arial;}, Arial is:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>font size</li>\r\n    <li>font style</li>\r\n    <li><strong>font family</strong></li>\r\n    <li>font weight</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>11. In the entry {padding: 10px 15px 20px 25px;} the top padding will be equal to:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>10px</strong></li>\r\n    <li>15px</li>\r\n    <li>20px</li>\r\n    <li>25px</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>12. In the Google Chrome browser, the default h1 tag size is:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>32px (2em)</strong></li>\r\n    <li>24px (1.5em)</li>\r\n    <li>16px (1em)</li>\r\n    <li>8px (0.5em)</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>13. In what format are styles written in the style tag?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>in HTML format</li>\r\n    <li>in JS format</li>\r\n    <li>in JSON format</li>\r\n    <li><strong>in CSS format</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>14. Select a value for the color property, written in HEX format, representing a deep blue color:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>#000000</li>\r\n    <li>#FF0000</li>\r\n    <li>#00FF00</li>\r\n    <li><strong>#0000FF</strong></li>\r\n    <li>#FFFFFF</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>15. Select the correct class-name class selector in the CSS:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>#class-name</li>\r\n    <li><strong>.class-name</strong></li>\r\n    <li>.class.name</li>\r\n    <li>class-name</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>16. Select the correct id-name selector in the CSS:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>.id-name</li>\r\n    <li>#id.name</li>\r\n    <li><strong>#id-name</strong></li>\r\n    <li>id-name</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>17. Select the correct values for the color property to indicate a deep red color:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>#FF0000</strong></li>\r\n    <li>#0000FF</li>\r\n    <li>rgb(0, 255, 0)</li>\r\n    <li><strong>rgb(255, 0, 0)</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>hsl(0, 100%, 50%)</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>18. Strikethrough text can be done using this text-decoration property value:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>none</li>\r\n    <li>underline</li>\r\n    <li>overline</li>\r\n    <li><strong>line-through</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>19. The animation is set using @keyframes. We need to set the animation duration to half a second. Which options will work?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>(1/2)s</li>\r\n    <li>calc(1/2)s</li>\r\n    <li><strong>0.5s</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>500ms</strong></li>\r\n    <li>0.0005ks</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>20. The degree of transparency in rgba recording varies within:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>from 0 to 1</strong></li>\r\n    <li>from 0 to 10</li>\r\n    <li>from 0 to F</li>\r\n    <li>from 0 to 255</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>20. The element has a set of properties {padding: 10px 20px; margin: 30px; border: 5px solid #040;}. What will be the total indentation to the right of the content?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>45</li>\r\n    <li>50</li>\r\n    <li><strong>55</strong></li>\r\n    <li>85</li>\r\n    <li>95</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>21. The element has properties {position: relative; top: 20px;}. Where will the element move relative to its current position by 20 pixels?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>top</li>\r\n    <li>right</li>\r\n    <li><strong>bottom</strong></li>\r\n    <li>left</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>22. The font, what does not have small strokes or extensions called \"serifs\" is</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>serif</li>\r\n    <li><strong>sans-serif</strong></li>\r\n    <li>cursive</li>\r\n    <li>monospace</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>23. The height of a div without text is determined by the property:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>width</li>\r\n    <li>line-height</li>\r\n    <li>high</li>\r\n    <li><strong>height</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>24. The parent element has the property {font-size: 2rem;}, and the child element has the property {font-size: 200%;}. What will be the font size of the child element in pixels?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>16px</li>\r\n    <li>24px</li>\r\n    <li>48px</li>\r\n    <li><strong>64px</strong></li>\r\n    <li>72px</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>25. The parent element's font size is 12px, and the child element's is 4em. What font size in pixels will the child element have?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>64px</li>\r\n    <li><strong>48px</strong></li>\r\n    <li>36px</li>\r\n    <li>32px</li>\r\n    <li>24px</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>26. The `z-index` property does not affect elements with position:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>relative</li>\r\n    <li>absolute</li>\r\n    <li>fixed</li>\r\n    <li><strong>static</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>27. These font weight options are not provided in CSS:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>0</strong></li>\r\n    <li>100</li>\r\n    <li>500</li>\r\n    <li>800</li>\r\n    <li><strong>1200</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>28. This value for the border-style property will set the element's border to be dotted:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>solid</li>\r\n    <li>double</li>\r\n    <li>dashed</li>\r\n    <li><strong>dotted</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>29. What property creates extra space around an element?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>border</li>\r\n    <li><strong>margin</strong></li>\r\n    <li>padding</li>\r\n    <li>box-sizing</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>29. Which of the following methods of style assignment has the highest specificity?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>selector by class</li>\r\n    <li><strong>style attribute inside the tag</strong></li>\r\n    <li>selector by id</li>\r\n    <li>selector by tag</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>30. Which of the following properties can use the value #aaa to set the background to gray?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>background-image</li>\r\n    <li><strong>background-color</strong></li>\r\n    <li>background-position</li>\r\n    <li>background-repeat</li>\r\n    <li><strong>background</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>31. Which property adjusts the space between letters of text?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>word-spacing</li>\r\n    <li>line-height</li>\r\n    <li>text-indent</li>\r\n    <li><strong>letter-spacing</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>32. You can make sure that all words in the text begin with a capital letter using this value of the text-transform property:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>none</li>\r\n    <li>uppercase</li>\r\n    <li><strong>capitalize</strong></li>\r\n    <li>lowercase</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>33. You can make the font italic (cursive or sloped) using these values ​​of the font-style property:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>none</li>\r\n    <li><strong>italic</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>oblique</strong></li>\r\n    <li>unset</li>\r\n    <li>normal</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n";
// Exports
/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = (code);

