// Module
var code = "<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <div id=\"link-to-quiz\" class=\"btn-back\">назад</div>\r\n\r\n  <h1>[St1] CSS Positioning & Flexbox</h1>\r\n\r\n  <strong>25 вопросов. Выполнил на 96 баллов из 100</strong>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>1. flex is a shorthand property where you can set 3 different properties: (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>flex-grow</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>flex-shrink</strong></li>\r\n    <li>flex-direction</li>\r\n    <li><strong>flex-basis</strong></li>\r\n    <li>flex-order</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>2. How to correctly add the flexbox property to a selected set of elements on the page?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Set \"display: flex\" to the parent element of the selected elements</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Set \"display: flex\" to each element that we want to turn into a flex item</li>\r\n    <li>Set \"display: flex\" for all elements on the page</li>\r\n    <li>Set \"display: flex\" to the html tag</li>\r\n    <li>Shout, 'Flex! I choose you!' and hope for the best</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>3. How to horizontally center a block element?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Set the element's width larger than the parent container's width and set the margins on the right and left to 'auto'</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Set the element's width smaller than the parent container's width and set the margins on the right and left to 'auto'</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Set the element's width smaller than the parent container's width and set the margins on the top and bottom to 'auto'</li>\r\n    <li>Set the element's width larger than the parent container's width and set the margins on the top and bottom to 'auto'</li>\r\n    <li>Ask it nicely to sit in the middle</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>4. How to style &lt;div&gt; elements to be arranged side by side horizontally from left to right? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>display: flex for the parent element</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>float: left</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>display: inline-block</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>5. Select the correct statements regarding position: absolute (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>An element with this positioning is removed from the main flow of the document</strong></li>\r\n    <li>An element with the value position: absolute is not a positioned element</li>\r\n    <li><strong>The element is placed relative to its nearest relatively positioned ancestor (if any)</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The element is positioned in the normal flow just like a static one, and then shifted using the properties left, right, top, bottom relative to the nearest scrolling parent</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>6. Select the correct statement regarding the align-content property:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>With this property, you can change the order of display of flex items inside the flex container</li>\r\n    <li><strong>The property distributes free space along the cross-axis between rows of flex items</strong></li>\r\n    <li>This property specifies whether a flex item can grow when there is free space and by how much</li>\r\n    <li>With this property, you can align one or several items differently than set on the parent element</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>7. The parent element, which is assigned the display: flex property, is called...</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>flex parent</li>\r\n    <li><strong>flex container</strong></li>\r\n    <li>flex item</li>\r\n    <li>main axis</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>8. What flex-direction property value should be specified so that child elements are arranged horizontally from left to right?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>column</li>\r\n    <li>column-reverse</li>\r\n    <li>row-reverse</li>\r\n    <li><strong>row</strong></li>\r\n    <li>moonwalk-mode (because Michael Jackson!)</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>9. What is the default value of the align-items property applied to the parent element for flex blocks?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>flex-start</li>\r\n    <li>flex-end</li>\r\n    <li>center</li>\r\n    <li><strong>stretch</strong></li>\r\n    <li>space-between</li>\r\n    <li>space-around</li>\r\n    <li>baseline</li>\r\n    <li>auto</li>\r\n    <li>random-dance-move</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>10. What is the default value of the align-self property applied to the parent element for flex blocks?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>flex-start</li>\r\n    <li>flex-end</li>\r\n    <li>center</li>\r\n    <li>stretch</li>\r\n    <li>space-between</li>\r\n    <li>space-around</li>\r\n    <li>baseline</li>\r\n    <li><strong>auto</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>11. What is the default value of the flex property?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>1 0 auto</li>\r\n    <li><strong>0 1 auto</strong></li>\r\n    <li>0 1 0</li>\r\n    <li>0 0 auto</li>\r\n    <li>0 0 0</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>12. What is the default value of the justify-content property applied to the parent element for flex blocks?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>flex-start</strong></li>\r\n    <li>flex-end</li>\r\n    <li>center</li>\r\n    <li>normal</li>\r\n    <li>stretch</li>\r\n    <li>space-between</li>\r\n    <li>space-around</li>\r\n    <li>baseline</li>\r\n    <li>auto</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>13. What statements about the block elements are correct? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>A line break is added before and after the element</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>You can set the width, height, padding, and margin for the element</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>The elements take up the full width of their parent (container)</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Block elements can contain inline elements, and cannot contain other block elements</li>\r\n    <li>The width and height of the element depend only on its content; you cannot set sizes using CSS</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>14. What statements about the inline elements are correct? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Line breaks are not added before and after the element</strong></li>\r\n    <li>You can set the width, height, padding, and margin for the element</li>\r\n    <li><strong>The width and height of the element depend only on its content; you cannot set sizes using CSS</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>The &lt;textarea&gt; tag is among them</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The elements take up the full width of their parent (container)</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>15. What type of positioning can an element have?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Static positioning</li>\r\n    <li>Relative positioning</li>\r\n    <li>Absolute positioning</li>\r\n    <li>Fixed positioning</li>\r\n    <li><strong>All of the above</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>16. Which elements are block-level by default? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>&lt;div&gt;</strong></li>\r\n    <li>&lt;i&gt;</li>\r\n    <li>&lt;span&gt;</li>\r\n    <li><strong>&lt;p&gt;</strong></li>\r\n    <li>&lt;a&gt;</li>\r\n    <li><strong>&lt;ul&gt;</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>&lt;li&gt;</strong></li>\r\n    <li>&lt;img&gt;</li>\r\n    <li><strong>&lt;table&gt;</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>17. Which elements are inline by default? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>&lt;p&gt;</li>\r\n    <li>&lt;table&gt;</li>\r\n    <li><strong>&lt;img&gt;</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>&lt;span&gt;</strong></li>\r\n    <li>&lt;li&gt;</li>\r\n    <li>&lt;ul&gt;</li>\r\n    <li>&lt;div&gt;</li>\r\n    <li><strong>&lt;i&gt;</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>&lt;a&gt;</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>18. Which of the listed properties allows flex items to wrap to a new line if they don't fit in the container?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>flex-sorter</li>\r\n    <li>flex-order</li>\r\n    <li><strong>flex-wrap</strong></li>\r\n    <li>flex-column</li>\r\n    <li>flex-direction</li>\r\n    <li>flex-tape</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>19. Which of the listed properties allows you to change the order of the flex items?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>flex-wrap</li>\r\n    <li>flex-sorter</li>\r\n    <li>flex-order</li>\r\n    <li>flex-column</li>\r\n    <li><strong>order</strong></li>\r\n    <li>sorter</li>\r\n    <li>column</li>\r\n    <li>wrap</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>20. Which properties does the shorthand property flex-flow contain?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Such property does not exist</li>\r\n    <li>flex-wrap and flex-shrink</li>\r\n    <li>flex-direction and flex-grow</li>\r\n    <li><strong>flex-direction and flex-wrap</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>21. Which property helps to hide an element from the page, as if it never existed?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>display: block</li>\r\n    <li>display: inline</li>\r\n    <li>display: inline-block</li>\r\n    <li>display: list-item</li>\r\n    <li><strong>display: none</strong></li>\r\n    <li>display: run-in</li>\r\n    <li>display: table</li>\r\n    <li>display: flex</li>\r\n    <li>display: magic-disappearo-trick</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>22. Which property is responsible for aligning elements along the main axis?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>justify-content</strong></li>\r\n    <li>align-content</li>\r\n    <li>flex-direction</li>\r\n    <li>align-items</li>\r\n    <li>align-self</li>\r\n    <li>flex: start</li>\r\n    <li>flex: stretch</li>\r\n    <li>compass</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>23. Which value(s) does the 'position' property not have? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>absolute</li>\r\n    <li>static</li>\r\n    <li>sticky</li>\r\n    <li><strong>normal</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>advanced</strong></li>\r\n    <li>relative</li>\r\n    <li>fixed</li>\r\n    <li><strong>none</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>24. Which value(s) for the 'position' property can an absolutely positioned element have? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>absolute</strong></li>\r\n    <li>static</li>\r\n    <li>sticky</li>\r\n    <li>normal</li>\r\n    <li>advanced</li>\r\n    <li>relative</li>\r\n    <li><strong>fixed</strong></li>\r\n    <li>none</li>\r\n    <li>subaquatic</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>25. Will the z-index work on an element without position (flex or grid aren't used)?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Yes, it will</li>\r\n    <li>Depends on the z-index value</li>\r\n    <li><strong>No, it won't</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Only if it's feeling on top of the world today</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n";
// Exports
