var code = "<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <div id=\"link-to-quiz\" class=\"btn-back\">назад</div>\r\n\r\n  <h1>[St1] CSS Grid</h1>\r\n\r\n  <strong>20 вопросов. Выполнил на 85 баллов из 100</strong>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>1. By default, a grid container behaves like a...?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>block element</strong></li>\r\n    <li>inline element</li>\r\n    <li>inline-block element</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>2. Can grid items occupy the same cell in CSS grids?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>No, grid items are always in separate cells</li>\r\n    <li>Yes, grid items can occupy the same cell</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Only if the parent grid has a specific setting</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Only if the grid items have the same class</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>3. How to assign a name to a grid area?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>grid-area: hd;</strong></li>\r\n    <li>grid-template-areas: \"hd hd hd\";</li>\r\n    <li>grid-area: hd 2 / 4 / 3 / 8;</li>\r\n    <li>none of the above</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>4. How to leave a grid cell empty?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>grid-template-areas: \"header - header header\";</li>\r\n    <li>grid-template-areas: \"header 0 header header\";</li>\r\n    <li><strong>grid-template-areas: \"header . header header\";</strong></li>\r\n    <li>grid-template-areas: \"header _ header header\";</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>5. In CSS grids, what does the value -1 typically represent when it comes to grid assignments?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>-1 is not a valid value in CSS grids</strong></li>\r\n    <li>-1 represents the first column or row in the grid</li>\r\n    <li>-1 is an alternate value for the very last column or row</li>\r\n    <li>-1 indicates a placeholder for empty grid cells</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>6. Is it possible to make an element a grid container using \"display: inline-grid\"?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Yes</strong></li>\r\n    <li>No</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>7. The \"grid-template\" property is a shorthand for properties:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>grid-template-rows</strong></li>\r\n    <li>grid-template-flow</li>\r\n    <li>grid-auto-flow</li>\r\n    <li><strong>grid-template-columns</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>grid-template-areas</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>8. The space between two adjacent grid lines (row or column) is called...</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Grid container</li>\r\n    <li>Grid line</li>\r\n    <li>Grid item</li>\r\n    <li>Grid area</li>\r\n    <li>Grid cell</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Grid track</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>9. What is the default behavior of an item in CSS Grid?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>The item will automatically span the entire grid</li>\r\n    <li>The item will not be displayed in the grid</li>\r\n    <li><strong>The item will span 1 track by default</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The item will span as many columns or rows as there are in the grid</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>10. What is the effect of setting the grid-template-columns to \"subgrid\" in a nested grid?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It creates a new set of columns for the nested grid</li>\r\n    <li><strong>The nested grid inherits the track definition from the parent grid</strong></li>\r\n    <li>It removes all columns from the nested grid</li>\r\n    <li>It applies a predefined layout to the nested grid</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>11. What is the space enclosed by four grid lines called?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Grid area</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Grid track</li>\r\n    <li>Grid cell</li>\r\n    <li>Grid line</li>\r\n    <li>Grid item</li>\r\n    <li>Grid container</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>12. What shorthand sets values for both \"align-items\" and \"justify-items\"?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>align-justify</li>\r\n    <li><strong>place-items</strong></li>\r\n    <li>grid-items</li>\r\n    <li>row-items</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>13. What values can be assigned to the grid-area property?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Any number of grid lines defining the location of the grid area</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Two grid lines to define the location of the grid area</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Four grid lines to define the location of the grid area</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Six grid lines to define the location of the grid area</li>\r\n    <li>A color code for the background color of the grid area</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>14. Which element becomes the parent when the \"display: grid\" property is applied?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Grid line</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Grid container</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Grid cell</li>\r\n    <li>Grid area</li>\r\n    <li>Grid track</li>\r\n    <li>Grid item</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>15. Which of the following statements about \"fr\" are correct?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>fr is a shorthand for fraction</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>fr is a unit of measurement</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>fr represents the free space within a grid container</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The code \"grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);\" creates one column that will take up 3 widths of the parent</li>\r\n    <li><strong>\"grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);\" and \"grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;\" are equivalent records</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>16. Which option is the shorthand for the statement: grid-template-columns: 150px 150px 150px;?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 150px);</strong></li>\r\n    <li>grid-template-columns: rep(150px, 3);</li>\r\n    <li>grid-columns: 150px * 3;</li>\r\n    <li>grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr, 150px;</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>17. Which property vertically aligns elements inside a grid container?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>justify-items</li>\r\n    <li>justify-content</li>\r\n    <li><strong>align-items</strong></li>\r\n    <li>place-items</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>18. Which syntax is used to name grid lines in CSS grid?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>grid-template-columns: [start] 1fr [middle] 2fr [end];</strong></li>\r\n    <li>grid-template-columns: start:: 1fr, middle:: 2fr, end:: 1fr;</li>\r\n    <li>grid-template-columns: 'start' 1fr 'middle' 2fr 'end';</li>\r\n    <li>grid-template-columns: &lt;start&gt; 1fr &lt;middle&gt; 2fr &lt;end&gt;;</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>19. Which statement is incorrect regarding the \"place-self\" property?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>The default value is center</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The value \"auto\" can be used to reset previously set values</li>\r\n    <li>If one value is specified, it is set for both properties</li>\r\n    <li>A shorthand property for \"justify-self\" and \"align-self\"</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>20. Which track sizes can you use to create a grid?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Fixed track sizes</li>\r\n    <li>Flexible track sizes</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Both of them</strong></li>\r\n    <li>None of them</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n";
// Exports
/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = (code);

