// Module
var code = "<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <div id=\"link-to-quiz\" class=\"btn-back\">назад</div>\r\n\r\n  <h1>[St1] CSS Modules And Some CSS New Features</h1>\r\n\r\n  <strong>27 вопросов. Выполнил на 81 баллов из 100</strong>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>1. Does CSS nesting represent pseudo-elements?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Not all of them, only :before and :after</li>\r\n    <li>Not all of them, only ::before and ::after</li>\r\n    <li><strong>No</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Yes</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>2. How does Anchor positioning work?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It positions an element as fixed at certain place on the page</li>\r\n    <li>It creates an anchor element in the corner of the page to be able to go to the top at any moment</li>\r\n    <li>It positions popover trigger element on the page</li>\r\n    <li><strong>It anchors an absolutely-positioned element to one or more other elements on the page</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>3. How to compose styles in CSS modules?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Import one CSS file to another</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Use 'composes' property to apply existing styles to the indicated selector in a new styles block</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Use compose() CSS function to apply existing styles to the indicated selector in a new styles block</li>\r\n    <li>There is no styles composition in CSS modules</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>4. How to style the third child within a parent element that has the \"container\" class, without concern for the impact on other elements' styles? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>.container:nth-child(3)</strong></li>\r\n    <li>.container::nth-child(3)</li>\r\n    <li><strong>.container:nth-child(2n+1)</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>.container:nth-child(odd)</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>5. How to switch to the global scope within a CSS Module?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>::global</li>\r\n    <li><strong>:global</strong></li>\r\n    <li>--global</li>\r\n    <li>:to-global</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>6. How trigonometric functions can be used in CSS?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>For animation, blueprints, etc.</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To satisfy your maths teacher by using trigonometry in your everyday life</li>\r\n    <li>For colors mixing</li>\r\n    <li>There are no Trigonometric functions in CSS</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>7. Is it possible to mix colors using CSS?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Yes, by using pseudo-class :mix-colors()</li>\r\n    <li>Yes, by using CSS function mix-color()</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Yes, by using CSS function color-mix()</strong></li>\r\n    <li>No</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>8. What are CSS Modules?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>A JavaScript file in which there are scripts for styles management</li>\r\n    <li><strong>A CSS file in which all class names and animation names are scoped locally by default</strong></li>\r\n    <li>A CSS file in which all class names and animation names are scoped globally by default</li>\r\n    <li>A block of styles in a CSS file</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>9. What are CSS viewport units?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Units which help size elements against the viewport size</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Units of viewport sizing used only in Media queries</li>\r\n    <li>Units for images sizing</li>\r\n    <li>Non of the above</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>10. What does the CSS pseudo-class :has() do?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>A built-in method of Array object for checking if value is included in array</li>\r\n    <li>A CSS pseudo-class which helps to check if selector has specific characters</li>\r\n    <li><strong>A CSS pseudo-class which allows to refine the main selector with an additional one</strong></li>\r\n    <li>A CSS pseudo-class which manages styles for elements when the user interacts with it by hovering it</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>11. What effects of interpolation exist for color-mix() in CSS?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>rgb, hex, pms, cmyk</li>\r\n    <li>completely, halfly, partly</li>\r\n    <li>linear, radial, repeating, conic</li>\r\n    <li><strong>lch, oklch, hsl, hwb, etc.</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>12. What functions are used for Anchor positioning? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>anchor()</strong></li>\r\n    <li>create-anchor()</li>\r\n    <li>set-anchor-size()</li>\r\n    <li><strong>anchor-size()</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>13. What HTML element can be a trigger for popover appearance?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Any HTML element with 'popover' attribute</li>\r\n    <li><strong>&lt;button&gt; or &lt;input type=\"button\"&gt; with 'popovertarget' attribute</strong></li>\r\n    <li>&lt;button&gt; or &lt;input type=\"button\"&gt; with 'popover' attribute</li>\r\n    <li>Any HTML element with 'popovertarget' attribute</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>14. What is a CSS nesting?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It's CSS function for styling nests</li>\r\n    <li><strong>It's a CSS feature which helps to get access to child elements to style them within parental style</strong></li>\r\n    <li>It's a CSS feature which gives an ability to nest one element into another</li>\r\n    <li>None of the above</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>15. What is a Dynamic viewport unit?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Viewport unit which represents the viewport height when the address bar UI hasn't shrunk its size yet</li>\r\n    <li>Viewport unit which represents the viewport height after the address bar UI shrunk its size</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Viewport unit which uses any of the small, in-between, and large units based on whether the address bar UI is shrunk or not</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Unit which is relative to the size of the initial containing block, which is the root element of a web page</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>16. What is a nesting selector?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>::</li>\r\n    <li>--</li>\r\n    <li>&&</li>\r\n    <li><strong>&</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>17. What is lvh?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Viewport unit which represents the viewport height when the address bar UI hasn't shrunk its size yet</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Viewport unit which represents the viewport height after the address bar UI shrunk its size</li>\r\n    <li>Viewport unit which is dynamic</li>\r\n    <li>It's CSS function</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>18. What is Popover?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>A global attribute used to designate an element as a popover element</strong></li>\r\n    <li>A HTML tag to create popover element</li>\r\n    <li>A HTML element which triggers popover appearance</li>\r\n    <li>A global attribute which converts any HTML element into popover trigger</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>19. What length units do Container Queries use?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>vh,vw, vmin, vmax</li>\r\n    <li>px, rem, em, %</li>\r\n    <li><strong>cqw, cqh, cqi, cqb, cqmin, cqmax</strong></li>\r\n    <li>All of the above</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>20. What statements about Anchor positioning are correct? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Anchor positioning helps to create tooltip or popover by anchoring it to target element using only HTML and CSS</li>\r\n    <li>It lets to create anchor-links to certain part of the page to use the, for example, in menu</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Anchored element can be positioned relative to its target element using 'anchor()' function in CSS file</strong></li>\r\n    <li>None of the above</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>21. What statements about composition in CSS modules are correct? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>You can compose styles to new selector from existing one</strong></li>\r\n    <li>You can't compose styles from different files</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Composition is very important for the DRY principle</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>You can use 'composes' property with styles in a current file or from another by passing the path to it</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>22. What statements about Container Queries are correct? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Container Queries is the same as Media Queries with the same syntax</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>@container rule lets style elements according to size of their parental container</strong></li>\r\n    <li>@container rule sets a certain element as container to other elements on the page</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Container Queries lets to create adaptive design without reference to viewport</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>23. What statements about modern CSS are correct? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Trigonometric functions are available for use in CSS</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>You can mix any colors using mix color function</strong></li>\r\n    <li>There are no new added features to CSS since releasing of Flexbox</li>\r\n    <li>CSS is about to be replaced with SCSS</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>24. What statements about Style Queries are correct? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It's HTML tag for managing application's styles</li>\r\n    <li><strong>The computed style of a parent element can be queried using style queries</strong></li>\r\n    <li>It's syntax style(computed_value)</li>\r\n    <li><strong>It works together with Container Queries</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>25. What statements about 'svh' are correct? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>It's a small viewport unit</strong></li>\r\n    <li>svh represents the viewport height when the address bar UI hasn't shrunk its size yet</li>\r\n    <li><strong>svh represents the viewport height after the address bar UI shrunk its size</strong></li>\r\n    <li>It's dynamic viewport</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>26. What Trigonometric functions are available in CSS?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>calc, min, max, translate, rotate</li>\r\n    <li>pow, sqrt, hypot, log, exp</li>\r\n    <li><strong>sin, cos, tan, asin, acos, atan, atan2</strong></li>\r\n    <li>There are no Trigonometric functions in CSS</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>27. What viewport units exist?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>cqw, cqh, cqi, cqb, cqmin, cqmax</li>\r\n    <li>px, rem, em, %</li>\r\n    <li><strong>vh,vw, vmin, vmax, svh, lvh, dvh</strong></li>\r\n    <li>All of the above</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n";
// Exports
/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = (code);

