// Module
var code = "<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <div id=\"link-to-quiz\" class=\"btn-back\">назад</div>\r\n\r\n  <h1>[St1] Final test stage#1</h1>\r\n\r\n  <strong>33 вопроса. Выполнил на 91 баллов из 100</strong>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>Are media queries case-sensitive?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>yes</li>\r\n    <li><strong>no</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>1. Class diagrams in UML:</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Are used to visualize and describe the dynamic aspects of a system or software application</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Are used to model the structure of object-oriented applications, including classes, their attributes, inheritance, class relationships, etc.</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Are used to know how objects interact with each other during a certain period of time and visualizes the timing constraints of a system</li>\r\n    <li>Focus on lifelines, or the processes and objects that live simultaneously, the messages exchanged between them and the order of the interaction</li>\r\n    <li>Are essentially a flowchart that shows activities performed by a system</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>2. Does the specification allow to add HTML tags after the &lt;body&gt; closing tag?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Yes, but these tags will be rendered after &lt;body&gt; in the DOM tree</li>\r\n    <li>Yes, but these tags will be rendered inside &lt;body&gt;</li>\r\n    <li>Yes, but they will not render</li>\r\n    <li>No, and such tags will not render</li>\r\n    <li><strong>No, but they will render inside &lt;body&gt;</strong></li>\r\n    <li>No, but they will render after &lt;body&gt; in the DOM tree</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>6. How does applying KISS principle benefit new team members?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Reduces onboarding time</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Increases code complexity</li>\r\n    <li>Encourages individual work</li>\r\n    <li>Limits creativity</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>3. How does webpack's 'mode' setting affect the build?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Determines the file types</li>\r\n    <li>Sets the language level</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Enables built-in optimizations</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Changes the output directory</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>4. How many times does a JS module code imports?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>After every re-render</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Only once, at the initial import</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Varies depending on the code structure</li>\r\n    <li>None of above</li>\r\n    <li>Whenever it feels like it needs a change of scenery</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>5. How to assign a name to a grid area?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>grid-area: hd;</strong></li>\r\n    <li>grid-template-areas: \"hd hd hd\";</li>\r\n    <li>grid-area: hd 2 / 4 / 3 / 8;</li>\r\n    <li>none of the above</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>6. I can’t find myself in the Total score and see how many points I have. How to do it?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Open the Score tab. In the table row after Github, click on the magnifying glass, enter your nickname on GitHub and press 'Enter'</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Open the Score tab. Sort everyone by name and view all pages in a row</li>\r\n    <li>Open the Score tab. Sort everyone by nickname in Github and view all pages in a row</li>\r\n    <li>Write to the #question-to-admins channel. They'll find it there right away</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>7. Identify the correct touch event types supported in JavaScript. (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>touchenter</li>\r\n    <li><strong>touchstart</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>touchmove</strong></li>\r\n    <li>touchleave</li>\r\n    <li><strong>touchend</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>touchcancel</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>14. In webpack, how does the 'filename' property within 'output' affect the build?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Sets up the code splitting strategy</li>\r\n    <li>Configures the public path</li>\r\n    <li>Determines module format</li>\r\n    <li>Instructs webpack on which files to exclude from bundling</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Defines the bundle name</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>8. In which element is the \"media\" attribute incorrectly specified?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>&lt;img src=\"flowers.jpg\" alt=\"flowers\" media=\"max: 500, min: 350\"&gt;</strong></li>\r\n    <li>&lt;link href=\"mobile.css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" media=\"screen and (max-width: 750px)\"&gt;</li>\r\n    <li>&lt;source srcset=\"flowers.jpg\" media=\"(max-width: 1400px)\"&gt;</li>\r\n    <li>&lt;a href=\"att_a_media.asp?output=print\" media=\"print and (resolution:300dpi)\"&gt;...&lt;/a&gt;</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>9. In which usage scenarios do Linked List and Array show significantly different operation execution speeds? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Accessing an arbitrary element by index</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Modifying an arbitrary element by index</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Outputting all list / array elements to the console</li>\r\n    <li>Removing an element from the list / array</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>10. Interaction diagrams in UML:</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Are used to know how objects interact with each other during a certain period of time and visualizes the timing constraints of a system</li>\r\n    <li>Focus on lifelines, or the processes and objects that live simultaneously, the messages exchanged between them and the order of the interaction</li>\r\n    <li>Are essentially a flowchart that shows activities performed by a system</li>\r\n    <li>Serve to model the structure of object-oriented applications, including classes, their attributes, inheritance, class relationships, etc.</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Are used to visualize and describe the dynamic aspects of a system or software application</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>11. Is the condition truthy: document.body.parentNode === document.documentElement?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Yes</strong></li>\r\n    <li>No</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>12. Select the correct statements: (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Static properties and methods of classes are inherited</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>A static method is declared using the 'static' keyword</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Static methods belong to a specific object of a class, not the class itself</li>\r\n    <li>Static properties are not inherited, but class methods are inherited</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>13. Select the valid control directives and loop expressions used in Sass: (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>@if</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>@for</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>@each</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>@while</strong></li>\r\n    <li>@goto</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>14. What commands can be used to make changes to the latest commit? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>git commit --amend --no-edit</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>git commit --amend</strong></li>\r\n    <li>git commit -am</li>\r\n    <li>git commit -m</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>15. What does destructuring assignment do?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>“Unpacks” arrays or objects into a bunch of variables</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Destroys an object provided as argument</li>\r\n    <li>Shows structure object passed as argument</li>\r\n    <li>Creates variables in a row using one keyword</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>16. What does 'IP' in 'IP address' stand for?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Intelligent Protocol</li>\r\n    <li>Incredible Pizza</li>\r\n    <li>Instant Pudding</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Internet Protocol</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>24. What is a dynamic import?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Module import in conditional statement</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Function-like expression that allows loading modules asynchronously</li>\r\n    <li>Re-exported imports</li>\r\n    <li>All of the above</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>17. What is a key feature of symmetric encryption?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Uses a different key for encryption and decryption</li>\r\n    <li>Is primarily used for hashing</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Uses the same key for encryption and decryption</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Operates only on text data</li>\r\n    <li>Involves a secret handshake</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>18. What is a .prettierrc file?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Configuration file used by Prettier</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Configuration file used by Node.js</li>\r\n    <li>Configuration file used by ESLint</li>\r\n    <li>File with this name doesn't exist</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>19. What is the difference between git fetch AND git pull</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>git fetch creates a new branch off the master branch, while git pull creates a new branch off the local repository's master branch.</li>\r\n    <li>git pull downloads new data from a remote repository without integrating it into local files, while git fetch updates the current HEAD branch with the latest changes from the remote server.</li>\r\n    <li>git fetch updates remote tracking branches with changes from a remote repository, while git pull updates remote tracking branches with changes from a remote repository and merges them into their corresponding local branches.</li>\r\n    <li>git fetch downloads and merges data from the local repository, while git pull informs your colleagues you are about to make changes to the master branch.</li>\r\n    <li><strong>None of these</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>19. What is the fundamental role of the Internet?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какова фундаментальная роль Интернета</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>A large storage system for data</li>\r\n    <li>A service provided by specific companies to access websites</li>\r\n    <li><strong>A large network of computers that communicate with each other</strong></li>\r\n    <li>A physical infrastructure spanning across continents</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>20. What is the result of: 2 + '2'?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>4</li>\r\n    <li>'4'</li>\r\n    <li><strong>'22'</strong></li>\r\n    <li>22</li>\r\n    <li>NaN</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>21. What is the result of: '6' * '3'?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>NaN</li>\r\n    <li>true</li>\r\n    <li><strong>18</strong></li>\r\n    <li>'18'</li>\r\n    <li>63</li>\r\n    <li>'63'</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>22. What is the result of: null===undefined?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>null</li>\r\n    <li>undefined</li>\r\n    <li>true</li>\r\n    <li><strong>false</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>21. What methods are available on a JavaScript event object? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>preventPropagation</li>\r\n    <li><strong>preventDefault</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>stopPropagation</strong></li>\r\n    <li>stopDefault</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>22. What method returns the value of the specified element attribute?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>hasAttribute()</li>\r\n    <li><strong>getAttribute()</strong></li>\r\n    <li>setAttribute()</li>\r\n    <li>attributes()</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>23. What statement is correct about attribute 'novalidate' for the &lt;form&gt; tag?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>This attribute doesn't exist</li>\r\n    <li><strong>It turns off automatic validation by browser and Constraint Validation API support</strong></li>\r\n    <li>It turns off automatic validation by browser and turns on Constraint Validation API support</li>\r\n    <li>It turns off built-in error messages and lets to add custom messages instead using JS</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>24. What statements about modern CSS are correct? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Trigonometric functions are available for use in CSS</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>You can mix any colors using mix color function</strong></li>\r\n    <li>There are no new added features to CSS since releasing of Flexbox</li>\r\n    <li>CSS is about to be replaced with SCSS</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>25. What will be the result of executing the code '\\nHey!'[1]?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>\\n</li>\r\n    <li>n</li>\r\n    <li><strong>H</strong></li>\r\n    <li>e</li>\r\n    <li>Uncaught SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>26. What will be the result of the code execution?\r\n    <br>function foo(a, b) {\r\n    <br>  return a * b;\r\n    <br>}\r\n    <br>const bar = foo.bind(null, 2);\r\n    <br>bar(2);\r\n  </h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>2</li>\r\n    <li><strong>4</strong></li>\r\n    <li>NaN</li>\r\n    <li>Will be an error</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>27. What will the code below output to the console?\r\n    <br>console.log(message);\r\n    <br>var message = 'Hello';</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>'Hello'</li>\r\n    <li><strong>undefined</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Will be an error</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>28. What will the code below output to the console?\r\n      <br>console.log(message);\r\n      <br>let message = 'Hello';</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>'Hello'</li>\r\n    <li>undefined</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Will be an error</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>29. Which data structure is most convenient for working with nested properties / parameters?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Set</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Map / Tree / Object</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Array</li>\r\n    <li>Linked List</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>30. Which graph traversal algorithm employs a queue?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Depth-First Search</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Breadth-First Search</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Binary Search</li>\r\n    <li>Merge Sort</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>31. Which of the following template categories, as defined by Luke Wroblewski, are commonly used in creating responsive web designs?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Mostly Fluid</li>\r\n    <li>Column Drop</li>\r\n    <li>Layout Shifter</li>\r\n    <li>Tiny Tweaks</li>\r\n    <li>Off Canvas</li>\r\n    <li>combinations of templates (e.g., Column Drop and Off Canvas)</li>\r\n    <li>none of the above</li>\r\n    <li><strong>all of them</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>32. Which of the following ways can you define a function to add two numbers in JavaScript? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>const sum = {a, b} => ( return a + b )</li>\r\n    <li><strong>const sum = (a, b) => { return a + b }</strong></li>\r\n    <li>const sum = {a, b} => a + b</li>\r\n    <li><strong>const sum = (a, b) => a + b</strong></li>\r\n    <li>const sum = a, b => a + b</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>21. Which property helps to hide an element from the page, as if it never existed?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>display: block</li>\r\n    <li>display: inline</li>\r\n    <li>display: inline-block</li>\r\n    <li>display: list-item</li>\r\n    <li><strong>display: none</strong></li>\r\n    <li>display: run-in</li>\r\n    <li>display: table</li>\r\n    <li>display: flex</li>\r\n    <li>display: magic-disappearo-trick</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>33. Which track sizes can you use to create a grid?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Fixed track sizes</li>\r\n    <li>Flexible track sizes</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Both of them</strong></li>\r\n    <li>None of them</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n";
// Exports
/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = (code);

