// Module
var code = "<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <div id=\"link-to-quiz\" class=\"btn-back\">назад</div>\r\n\r\n  <h1>Git test</h1>\r\n\r\n  <strong>33 вопроса. Выполнил 100 балл из 100. Это правлиьных 31 ответов</strong>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>1. How are the user name and email set for commit identification?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Как задаются имя пользователя и адрес электронной почты для идентификации фиксации</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>With the git set user.name (user.email) command</li>\r\n    <li><strong>With the git config user.name (user.email) command</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The user name and email are taken from the GitHub account associated with the current SSH key</li>\r\n    <li>The user name and email are contained in the current SSH key and are used for each subsequent commit</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>2. How to fix the error \"fatal: The current branch my-branch has no upstream branch\", which occurs when using git push and set up a local branch to track a remote branch so that the error does not occur in the future when using git push?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Как исправить ошибку «фатальная: текущая ветка my-branch не имеет восходящей ветки», которая возникает при использовании git push и настроить локальную ветку для отслеживания удаленной ветки, чтобы ошибка не возникала в будущем при использовании git push</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>git push -n origin my-branch</li>\r\n    <li><strong>git push -u origin my-branch</strong></li>\r\n    <li>git push -f origin my-branch</li>\r\n    <li>git push origin my-branch</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>3. What command creates a new commit that applies changes that are opposite to the commit specified as the argument?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какая команда создает новую commit, которая применяет изменения, противоположные фиксации, указанной в качестве аргумента</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>git reset --mixed</li>\r\n    <li>git reset --soft</li>\r\n    <li><strong>git revert</strong></li>\r\n    <li>git commit --amend</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>4. What command creates a new branch with the name “feature/new-feature” and automatically switches to it?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какая команда создает новую ветку с названием «feature/new-feature» и автоматически переключается на нее</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>git branch feature/new-feature</li>\r\n    <li>git branch -b feature/new-feature</li>\r\n    <li><strong>git checkout -b feature/new-feature</strong></li>\r\n    <li>git checkout feature/new-feature</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>5. What command displays the commit history of the current branch?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какая команда отображает историю коммитов текущей ветки</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>git log</strong></li>\r\n    <li>git show</li>\r\n    <li>git status</li>\r\n    <li>git diff</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>6. What command displays the URLs of the remote repositories, indicating the protocol used?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какая команда отображает URL-адреса удаленных репозиториев с указанием используемого протокола</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>git remote -v</strong></li>\r\n    <li>git remote -s</li>\r\n    <li>git remote -p</li>\r\n    <li>git remote -l</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>7. What command is used to create a copy of a remote repository?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какая команда используется для создания копии удаленного репозитория</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>git fetch</li>\r\n    <li>git pull</li>\r\n    <li><strong>git clone</strong></li>\r\n    <li>git add</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>8. What command is used to create a new local repository?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какая команда используется для создания нового локального репозитория</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>git fetch</li>\r\n    <li>git pull</li>\r\n    <li>git clone</li>\r\n    <li><strong>git init</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>9. What command is used to send the state of the current local branch to the remote repository?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какая команда используется для отправки состояния текущей локальной ветки в удаленный репозиторий</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>git upload</li>\r\n    <li>git pull</li>\r\n    <li><strong>git push</strong></li>\r\n    <li>git update</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>10. What command is used to switch between branches or move the pointer to another existing commit?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какая команда используется для переключения между ветками или перемещения указателя на другой существующий коммит</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>git branch</li>\r\n    <li>git select</li>\r\n    <li>git checkout -b</li>\r\n    <li><strong>git checkout</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>11. What command outputs the changes made by a specific commit?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какая команда выводит изменения, внесенные конкретным коммитом</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>git changes</li>\r\n    <li><strong>git show</strong></li>\r\n    <li>git status</li>\r\n    <li>git diff</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>12. What commands can be used to make changes to the latest commit?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какие команды можно использовать для внесения изменений в последний коммит</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>git commit --amend --no-edit</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>git commit --amend</strong></li>\r\n    <li>git commit -am</li>\r\n    <li>git commit -m</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>13. What commands can move the current pointer to the specified commit without changing the files in the working directory?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какие команды могут переместить текущий указатель на указанный коммит без изменения файлов в рабочем каталоге</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>git checkout</li>\r\n    <li>git reset --hard</li>\r\n    <li><strong>git reset --soft</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>git reset</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>14. What does git rebase -i allow?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Что позволяет делать git rebase -i</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Allows you to rewrite the history of the branch specified in the argument, starting from the commit where the current branch's branching occurred, as the -i key means inversed</li>\r\n    <li>Allows selective merging of the history of the current and specified branches</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Allows during a normal rebase to choose the commits that will remain in the branch after the command is executed</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Allows during a normal rebase to edit changes in one or more commits</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>15. What does the git add command do?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Что делает команда git add</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Loads a local file into the remote repository so that other project participants can see it</li>\r\n    <li>Creates a file with the specified name and immediately starts tracking it</li>\r\n    <li>Saves the current prepared changes to the local repository</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Allows Git to start tracking files and also adds current changes to the staging area</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>16. What does the git branch command do?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Что делает команда git Branch</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Outputs the changes between the local and remote version of the current branch</li>\r\n    <li>Switches to the branch whose name is specified as an argument</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Outputs a list of branches in the current local repository</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Creates a new branch with the name specified as an argument</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>17. What does the git cherry-pick command do?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Что делает команда git Cherry-Pick</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>The git cherry-pick command is used to copy a specific commit from one branch to another, applying the changes introduced in that commit. Создает новый коммит в текущей ветке, содержащий изменения из указанного коммита</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The git cherry-pick command is a secret code for initiating the self-destruct sequence</li>\r\n    <li>The git cherry-pick command combines the changes from several commits into one before applying it to the current branch</li>\r\n    <li>The git cherry-pick command deletes a specific commit from the history</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>18. What does the git commit command do by default?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Что делает команда git commit по умолчанию</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Saves all changes in the working directory to the local repository</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Saves changes made to the staging area to the local repository</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Sends the current local changes to the remote repository</li>\r\n    <li>Creates a comment for the current changes</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>19. What does the git commit command with the -am flag do?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Что делает команда git commit с флагом -am</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Saves all changes in the working directory, including all untracked files, to the local repository</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Saves all changes, both staged and unstaged, for all tracked files and also updates the commit message</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Uploads the current local changes to the remote repository</li>\r\n    <li>Creates a new branch and moves the current changes to that branch</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>20. What does the git rm command do?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Что делает команда git rm</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Deletes a branch</li>\r\n    <li>Deletes a commit</li>\r\n    <li>Removes changes from a given commit</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Removes files with changes from the working directory and the index</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>21. What happens when you run the git fetch command?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Что происходит, когда вы запускаете команду git fetch</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Data from the local repository will be uploaded to the remote repository</li>\r\n    <li>A copy of the remote repository will be created</li>\r\n    <li>Data from the remote repository will be copied to the local repository, updating the data of the current local branch</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Data from the remote repository will be copied to the local repository without changing the current state of the local branch</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>22. What is a Pull Request on GitHub?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Что такое Pull Request в GitHub?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>A notification to project participants to download the updated branch version from the remote repository using the git pull command.</li>\r\n    <li><strong>A request to merge your changes from your branch or repository into another branch or repository. Your changes will be reviewed and discussed before merging.</strong></li>\r\n    <li>A request to project participants to have someone complete the functionality development / fix a bug in your branch.</li>\r\n    <li>A section that allows to merge branches on GitHub without using the local repository and terminal.</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>23. What is Git?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Что такое Git</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Cloud data storage</li>\r\n    <li>Console utility for working with files</li>\r\n    <li>Console utility for creating a backup of files</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Version control system</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>24. What is GitHub?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Что такое GitHub</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Cloud data storage</li>\r\n    <li>Program for working with Git</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Web service for hosting projects and their collaborative development, based on Git</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Storage of file backups</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>25. What is the difference between the master branch and origin/master?</h3>\r\n  <h3>В чем разница между master веткой и origin/master</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Master belongs to the local repository, while origin/master belongs to the remote repository</strong></li>\r\n    <li>These are two different branches of the same repository</li>\r\n    <li>Master and origin/master are two names for the same branch</li>\r\n    <li>The origin/master branch does not exist because the name contains an incorrect symbol</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>26. What is the name of the pointer to the current state in the branch?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Как называется указатель на текущее состояние в ветке</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>CURRENT</li>\r\n    <li>TOP</li>\r\n    <li><strong>HEAD</strong></li>\r\n    <li>SELECTED</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>27. What is the purpose of the .gitignore file?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какова цель файла .gitignore</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>To exclude files and directories when working with Git</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To make Git work correctly</li>\r\n    <li>Because there is nothing useful in there</li>\r\n    <li>To exclude branches and commits when working with Git</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>28. What will happen during a git rebase without conflicts?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Что произойдет во время git rebase без конфликтов</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>The merging of commit history from the specified branch into the current branch based on the commit date</li>\r\n    <li>The overlay of commit history from the specified branch onto the end of the current branch history</li>\r\n    <li><strong>The overlay of commit history from the current branch onto the end of the specified branch history</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The rewriting of the current branch history by recreating commits, which will begin from the end of the specified branch</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>29. What will happen when the git pull command is executed?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Что произойдет, когда будет выполнена команда git pull</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Data from the local repository will be uploaded to the remote repository</li>\r\n    <li>A copy of the remote repository will be created</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Data from the remote repository will be copied to the local repository, updating the data of the current local branch</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Data from the remote repository will be copied to the local repository without changing the current state of the local branch</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3 style=\"color: brown;\">30. What will happen when you run git merge without conflicts?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Что произойдет, если вы запустите git merge без конфликтов</h3>\r\n  --------------\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Был первый ответ A new commit will be created in the current branch with all the changes from the specified branch</li>\r\n    <li><strong>The history of commits from the specified branch will be merged into the current branch by date with the addition of a merge commit</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The changes from the specified branch will be applied to the current branch without creating a new commit</li>\r\n    <li>A new branch with all the changes from the specified branch will be created</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>31. What's the difference between Git's local and global configurations?</h3>\r\n  <h3>В чем разница между локальной и глобальной конфигурациями Git</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Local is applied for the current OS user, global is for all users</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Local is applied for the current local repository, global is for all repositories if there is no local config</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Local is applied for the current branch, global is for all branches</li>\r\n    <li>Local is applied for the current OS locale</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>32. Which command displays the status of files in the working directory and the staging area?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какая команда показывает состояние файлов в рабочей директории и staging area, какие файлы изменены, но не добавлены в staging area, а какие уже ожидают коммита, находясь в staging area?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>git log</li>\r\n    <li>git show</li>\r\n    <li><strong>git status</strong></li>\r\n    <li>git diff</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3 style=\"color: brown;\"\">33. Which command displays uncommitted changes compared to the last commit in the current branch?</h3>\r\n  <h3>Какая команда отображает незафиксированные изменения по сравнению с последней фиксацией в текущей ветке</h3>\r\n  --------------\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>git changes</li>\r\n    <li>git show</li>\r\n    <li>первый ответ git status</li>\r\n    <li><strong>git diff</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n";
// Exports
/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = (code);

