// Module
var code = "<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <div id=\"link-to-quiz\" class=\"btn-back\">назад</div>\r\n\r\n  <h1>Test [St1] Linters, Formatters and Husky</h1>\r\n\r\n  <strong>33 вопроса. Выполнил на 85 баллов из 100</strong>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>1. How can ESLint be configured? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>By enabling a rule as a warning or an error</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>By creation of custom rules</strong></li>\r\n    <li>By add code quality analytics</li>\r\n    <li>By integrating linting into a build process</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>2. How do you configure plugins in an ESLint configuration file?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Using the 'eslint-config' key</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Using the 'plugins' key</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Directly in the 'rules' section</li>\r\n    <li>In the '.eslintrc' file's header</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>3. How does Husky works?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It checks if a relevant Git Hook is available for a called Git command</li>\r\n    <li>It formats code to comply with code style requirements</li>\r\n    <li><strong>It runs a Git Hook when a relevant Git command is called</strong></li>\r\n    <li>It scans code to indicate all problems with code quality</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>4. Is ESLint capable of formatting code?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Yes, without any limits</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Yes, but Prettier is a more capable tool for this purpose</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Yes, but Husky is a more relevant tool for this purpose</li>\r\n    <li>Absolutely not</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>5. Is it mandatory to use linters, formatters, Husky in project?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Yes, everything is mandatory</li>\r\n    <li>Only linters and Husky are mandatory</li>\r\n    <li>Only formatters are mandatory</li>\r\n    <li><strong>They're not mandatory but highly recommended to keep a good code quality</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>6. In which file is Husky's command configuration stored after running 'husky-init'?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>package.json</strong></li>\r\n    <li>.eslintrc.* (or eslint.config.js.)</li>\r\n    <li>.prettierrc</li>\r\n    <li>.huskyrc</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>7. What are benefits of using ESLint? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Objective measurement of a code quality</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Readable, maintainable, and more consistent code</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Fewer errors in production</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Education about code quality reaches more app users</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>8. What are Code Smells?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>The processes of verifying codebases for adherence to code styles</li>\r\n    <li>Errors in code after compilation</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Signs that something might be wrong with a code</strong></li>\r\n    <li>All of the above</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>9. What are code style guides created for?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>To design application UI in a unified style</li>\r\n    <li><strong>To help developers write consistent and maintainable code</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To simplify code writing by accumulation of typical code blocks</li>\r\n    <li>Style guides are created for UI/UX designers</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>10. What are ESLint rules?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Open list of rules for code checks, set up in package.json</li>\r\n    <li>Predefined list of rules for code checks, set up in package.json</li>\r\n    <li>Open list of rules for code checks, set up in ESLint configuration file</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Predefined list of rules for code checks, set up in ESLint configuration file</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>11. What are features of Husky? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Zero dependencies and lightweight</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>User-friendly messages</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Husky supports platforms such as macOS, Linux, and Windows</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Powered by modern new Git feature (core.hooksPath)</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>12. What can Husky do? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Run any command, for example from one of the installed packages (e.g. Prettier)</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Use 'pre-commit' script to run all tests</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Validate commit messages</li>\r\n    <li>Fix code smells before pushing the commit</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>13. What do an ESLint rule with a value 'error' in case of any error?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It crashes an app</li>\r\n    <li><strong>It shows an error message in the terminal with a path to a file with the error</strong></li>\r\n    <li>It shows only an error message</li>\r\n    <li>It shows a number of errors in an app</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>14. What does a .eslintrc.* (or eslint.config.js.) file represent?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Configuration file used by Prettier</li>\r\n    <li>Configuration file used by Node.js</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Configuration file used by ESLint</strong></li>\r\n    <li>File with this name doesn't exist</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>15. What does an ESLint rule with a value 'warn' do?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>It shows a warning in the terminal with a path to a problematic file</strong></li>\r\n    <li>It shows an error message</li>\r\n    <li>It provides analytics with all warnings</li>\r\n    <li>It does nothing</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>16. What does setting 'singleQuote' to true do in Prettier?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Forces the use of double quotes</li>\r\n    <li>Enables single quotes in JSX</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Uses single quotes instead of double quotes</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Disables quote conversion</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>17. What does the 'eslint-plugin-' prefix in ESLint plugin names indicate?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It's a mandatory prefix for all ESLint plugins</li>\r\n    <li><strong>It can be omitted from plugin names in configuration</strong></li>\r\n    <li>It's only used for scoped packages</li>\r\n    <li>Indicates a deprecated plugin</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>18. What does the 'semi' option in Prettier control?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>The insertion of semicolons at the end of statements</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Checking for missing semicolons</li>\r\n    <li>Conversion of double quotes to semicolons</li>\r\n    <li>The style of semicolons used</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>19. What Git hooks from the list really exists? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>pre-commit</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>pre-push</strong></li>\r\n    <li>pre-pull</li>\r\n    <li><strong>pre-rebase</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>20. What is a linter?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>A tool for improving code quality</strong></li>\r\n    <li>A tool for formatting new code before a commit to be created</li>\r\n    <li>A modern native Git hooks tool</li>\r\n    <li>None of the above</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>21. What is a linter used for? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Fix programming errors</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Code standardization</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Adapting legacy code for modern browsers</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Identify bugs</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>22. What is a .prettierrc file?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Configuration file used by Prettier</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Configuration file used by Node.js</li>\r\n    <li>Configuration file used by ESLint</li>\r\n    <li>File with this name doesn't exist</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>23. What is Husky? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>JavaScript library</li>\r\n    <li>The most popular code formatter</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Tool for automation of adding Git Hooks</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>24. What is Prettier?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>A bugs highlighter</li>\r\n    <li>A pre-commit hook</li>\r\n    <li>A linter</li>\r\n    <li><strong>A code formatter</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>25. What is the default value for Prettier's 'printWidth' option?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>80 characters</strong></li>\r\n    <li>100 characters</li>\r\n    <li>120 characters</li>\r\n    <li>No default value</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>26. What statements are correct about Prettier and ESLint integration? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Integration of this tools gives opportunity to run them together as one job</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Prettier provides 'eslint-plugin-prettier' and 'eslint-config-prettier' rules to accomplish this</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Prettier's config can be defined in a .eslintrc.* (or eslint.config.js.) file when these tools are used together</strong></li>\r\n    <li>These tools can't be integrated with each other</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>27. What types of checks do a linter provide? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Syntax errors</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Potential problems</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Number of warnings in console</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Code standards adherence</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>28. What values can be set to ESLint rules?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>'off', 'on'</li>\r\n    <li><strong>'off', 'warn', 'error'</strong></li>\r\n    <li>'ignore', 'warn', 'error'</li>\r\n    <li>'disable', 'enable'</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>29. Which coding style guides are most popular? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Airbnb</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Netflix</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Google</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Idiomatic</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The Rolling Scopes School</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>30. Which of the following Git hooks are not supported by Husky? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>pre-receive</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>update</strong></li>\r\n    <li>pre-push</li>\r\n    <li><strong>post-receive</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>31. Which of the following is true about the 'tabWidth' option in Prettier? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Specifies the number of characters per indentation-level</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Defaults to 4 spaces</li>\r\n    <li>Is used to set the width of tabs in the output file</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Controls the number of spaces in a tab character</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>32. Which option in Prettier is used to control trailing commas?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>'commaStyle'</li>\r\n    <li><strong>'trailingComma'</strong></li>\r\n    <li>'commaEnd'</li>\r\n    <li>'endComma'</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>33. Why is a good practice to use ESLint together with Prettier?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Prettier is able only detect problems in code, ESLint fix it</li>\r\n    <li>Prettier makes ESLint warnings and errors more readable for users</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Prettier enforces a consistent code style and linter/ESLint is responsible for code-quality rules and catching bugs</strong></li>\r\n    <li>ESLint identifies issues but cannot fix all, Prettier can</li>\r\n    <li>There is no difference between ESLint and Prettier and it's not necessary to use them together</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n";
// Exports
/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = (code);

