var code = "<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <div id=\"link-to-quiz\" class=\"btn-back\">назад</div>\r\n\r\n  <h1>[St1] Preprocessors. SASS</h1>\r\n\r\n  <strong>28 вопросов. Выполнил на 86 баллов из 100</strong>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>1. Can colors be mixed in Sass using the mix function like `color: mix(red, blue)`?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong></strong>Yes</strong></li>\r\n    <li>No</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>2. Can string values in Sass be used without quotes?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Yes</strong></li>\r\n    <li>No</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>3. Choose the correct spellings for the nested rules:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>.article{ .title{ color: red; }}</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>.article{ &.title{ color: red; }}</strong></li>\r\n    <li>.article{ &&.title{ color: red; }}</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>4. Choose the correct statement:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>The CSS file can be renamed to SCSS and it will still be valid</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The CSS file can be renamed to SASS and it will still be valid</li>\r\n    <li>All statements are incorrect</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>5. How are placeholder selectors called correctly?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>@include title;</li>\r\n    <li>@import title;</li>\r\n    <li>@extend title;</li>\r\n    <li><strong>@extend %title;</strong></li>\r\n    <li>@import %title;</li>\r\n    <li>@include %title;</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>6. How do you declare a local variable as global within its scope?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>$width: 5em global;</li>\r\n    <li><strong>$width: 5em !global;</strong></li>\r\n    <li>$width: 5em !glob;</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>7. How is a variable declared correctly in SASS?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>$width: 5em;</strong></li>\r\n    <li>width: 5em;</li>\r\n    <li>$width = 5em;</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>8. How is a variable declared with a default value in SASS?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>$width: 5em default;</li>\r\n    <li>$width: 5em;</li>\r\n    <li><strong>$width: 5em !default;</strong></li>\r\n    <li>$width: 5em !=default;</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>9. Identify the valid Sass rules and directives from the list below:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>@import</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>@media</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>@extend</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>@at-root</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>@debug</strong></li>\r\n    <li>@try</li>\r\n    <li>@catch</li>\r\n    <li>@warning</li>\r\n    <li><strong>@warn</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>@error</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>10. In Sass, the `&`operator is used to...</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>link to parent</strong></li>\r\n    <li>logical AND</li>\r\n    <li>reference to the value of a variable in memory</li>\r\n    <li>There is no correct answer</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>11. Is it possible to use parentheses in expressions?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>You cannot use parentheses in expressions</li>\r\n    <li>Parentheses do not affect the order of operations in expressions</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Parentheses can be used to determine the order of actions in expressions</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>12. Is it possible to use variable interpolations in comments?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Yes</strong></li>\r\n    <li>No</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>13. Is the following code valid: `.funky { font: 20px/24px fantasy {weight: bold;}}`?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>No</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Yes</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>14. Lists do not support any special operations. There are list functions to work with them. Is the statement true?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Yes</strong></li>\r\n    <li>No</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>15. Select SASS benefits:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Fully CSS compatible</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Rich functionality</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Industry support</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Great community</strong></li>\r\n    <li>BEM</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>16. Select supported data types in SassScript:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>numbers</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>text strings</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>colors</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>null</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>lists of values</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>arrays (Maps)</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Heaps</li>\r\n    <li>undefined</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>17. Select the correct statements regarding maps in Sass:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Unlike lists, maps must always be enclosed in parentheses and must always be separated by commas</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Maps are the same as lists</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Keys and values in maps can be any SassScript objects</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Keys and values in maps can only be strings</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>18. Select the correct statements regarding operations in SassScript:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>All data types support equality operators ( == and != )</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>SassScript allows you to perform mathematical operations with different types (1px + 2rem + 3em + 4vh)</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Comparison operators ( &lt;, &gt;, &lt;=, &gt;=, ==, != ) are also supported for numbers</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>SassScript supports standard arithmetic operations on numbers (+, -, *, /, %).</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>10px * 3px is a valid operation</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>19. Select the correct statement regarding Sass's compressed output mode:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>In compression mode, Sass will output what is written in sass as it is</li>\r\n    <li><strong>In compressed mode, Sass will output style written in a single line without extra characters and with the smallest CSS representation of the color</strong></li>\r\n    <li>There is no right answer</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>20. Select the valid control directives and loop expressions used in Sass:</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>@if</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>@for</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>@each</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>@while</strong></li>\r\n    <li>@goto</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>21. What is the correct syntax for interpolation in SassScript?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>`@{$var}`</li>\r\n    <li><strong>`#{$var}`</strong></li>\r\n    <li>`${$var}`</li>\r\n    <li>There is no correct answer</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>22. What is the result of this `content: \"Foo \" + Bar;` operation?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>content: \"Foo Bar\";</strong></li>\r\n    <li>content: Foo Bar;</li>\r\n    <li>The</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>23. What is the syntax for AND, OR, and NOT logical operators in SassScript?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>and, or, not</strong></li>\r\n    <li>&&, ||, !</li>\r\n    <li>Such operators are not supported</li>\r\n    <li>There is no correct answer</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>24. Which command enables interactive mode for SASS in the console?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>npm run sass -i</li>\r\n    <li><strong>sass -i</strong></li>\r\n    <li>sass -interactive</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  re is no correct answer</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>25. Which comment will always remain in the compiled CSS even after compression?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>// Something important</li>\r\n    <li>//! Something important</li>\r\n    <li><strong>/* Something important */</strong></li>\r\n    <li>/*! Something important */</li>\r\n    <li>&lt;-- Something important --&gt;</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>26. Which entry for placeholder selectors is correct?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>.title{color:red}</li>\r\n    <li>#title{color:red}</li>\r\n    <li><strong>%title{color:red}</strong></li>\r\n    <li>@title{color:red}</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>27. Which of the following are valid ways to call the hsl function in Sass?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>`hsl($hue: 0, $saturation: 100%, $lightness: 50%)`</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>`hsl(0, 100%, 50%)`</strong></li>\r\n    <li>`hsl( $lightness: 50%, $hue: 0, $saturation: 100%)`</li>\r\n    <li>There is no correct answer</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>28. Which operators are available for working with lists in Sass?</h3>\r\n\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>map</li>\r\n    <li><strong>nth</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>append</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>join</strong></li>\r\n    <li>merge</li>\r\n    <li>as</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n";
// Exports
/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = (code);

