// Module
var code = "<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <div id=\"link-to-quiz\" class=\"btn-back\">назад</div>\r\n\r\n  <h1>[St2] Single Page Application</h1>\r\n\r\n  <strong>33 вопроса. Выполнил на 88 баллов из 100</strong>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>1. How do SPAs typically handle data updates on the page?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Sending a fax to the server</li>\r\n    <li>By updating the entire website</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Using JavaScript to update only parts of the page</strong></li>\r\n    <li>By getting another standalone page with data from the server</li>\r\n    <li>By reloading the entire page</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>2. How does Location.assign() method function?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>It assigns homework to web developers</li>\r\n    <li>It opens a new browser window</li>\r\n    <li><strong>It loads the resource at the given URL</strong></li>\r\n    <li>It reloads the current document</li>\r\n    <li>It replaces the current document with a new one without adding to history</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>3. In web development, what is a practical use of the History API?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Storing user data</li>\r\n    <li>Creating animations</li>\r\n    <li>Tracking user location</li>\r\n    <li>Organizing online historical reenactments</li>\r\n    <li>Managing browser history navigation</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Optimizing website loading speed</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>4. What are Server-Sent Events (SSEs) used for in SPAs?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Client-to-server communication</li>\r\n    <li>Implementing data encryption</li>\r\n    <li>Managing user sessions</li>\r\n    <li>Load balancing between servers</li>\r\n    <li>Facilitating movie streaming services</li>\r\n    <li>Persisting data within the client-side storage</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Sending data from server to client in real time</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>5. What does AJAX stand for in the context of SPAs?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Always Joking and eXaggerating</li>\r\n    <li>Automatic Java and XHTML</li>\r\n    <li>Asynchronous Java and XML</li>\r\n    <li>Advanced JavaScript and XML</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Asynchronous JavaScript and XML</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>6. What does the Location.origin property provide?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>The hostname of the URL</li>\r\n    <li>The secret location of the lost city of Atlantis</li>\r\n    <li>The coordinates of the International Space Station</li>\r\n    <li><strong>The protocol, hostname and port of the URL</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The port number of the URL</li>\r\n    <li>The pathname of the URL</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>7. What does the Location.pathname property return?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>The path of the URL</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The protocol of the URL</li>\r\n    <li>The fragment identifier of the URL</li>\r\n    <li>The latest trending path on social media</li>\r\n    <li>The query string of the URL</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>8. What does the Location.search property return?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>The protocol of the URL</li>\r\n    <li>The secret search history of the user</li>\r\n    <li><strong>A '?' followed by the parameters of the URL</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The search results for the current URL</li>\r\n    <li>The hostname of the URL</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>9. What does the 'pushState()' method in the History API do?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Adds a new entry to the history stack</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Updates the current history entry</li>\r\n    <li>Deletes the current history entry</li>\r\n    <li>Sends a push notification</li>\r\n    <li>Replaces the current history entry with a new one</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>10. What does the 'replaceState()' method in the History API do?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Updates the most recent entry on the history stack</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Swaps history with an alternate universe</li>\r\n    <li>Saves the current page as a bookmark</li>\r\n    <li>Replaces the current page with a new one</li>\r\n    <li>Deletes all history entries</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>11. What functionality does the 'go()' method provide in the History API?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Teleports you to the past</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Loads a specific page from session history based on relative position</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Opens a new browser window</li>\r\n    <li>Changes the color of the browser</li>\r\n    <li>Sends an email</li>\r\n    <li>Closes the current browser tab</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>12. What is a common issue faced by SPAs in terms of SEO?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>They are incompatible with major search engines</li>\r\n    <li>They are always ranked first in search engines</li>\r\n    <li>They only appear in searches made on weekends</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Their dynamic content can be harder for search engines to index</strong></li>\r\n    <li>They tend to overheat search engines</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>13. What is a key characteristic of SPAs in terms of page loading?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>They teleport users to a parallel universe</li>\r\n    <li>They require the entire page to be reloaded for every action</li>\r\n    <li><strong>They load all content on the initial page load, then dynamically update</strong></li>\r\n    <li>They never need to be reloaded</li>\r\n    <li>They only load text, not images or videos</li>\r\n    <li>Lazy loading of resources</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>14. What is a major benefit of SPAs?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>They use less JavaScript</li>\r\n    <li>They don't require a web server</li>\r\n    <li>They are easier to debug</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Faster transitions and a more app-like experience</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>15. What is a single-page application (SPA)?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>An offline desktop application</li>\r\n    <li>A web application that requires constant page refreshing</li>\r\n    <li>A website that only contains one page</li>\r\n    <li>An application downloaded from an app store for mobile devices</li>\r\n    <li><strong>A web application that dynamically updates the current page with new data from the web server, without reloading</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>16. What is a valid method for advancing forward in the browsing history using the History API?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Using a time machine</li>\r\n    <li>history.fastForward()</li>\r\n    <li>history.proceed()</li>\r\n    <li>history.skip()</li>\r\n    <li><strong>history.forward()</strong></li>\r\n    <li>history.moveForward()</li>\r\n    <li>history.next()</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>17. What is an important prerequisite before learning client-side frameworks?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Having a degree in computer science</li>\r\n    <li>Understanding quantum physics</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Knowing the basics of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Mastering graphic design</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>18. What is one major advantage of using a JavaScript framework?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>They work without an internet connection</li>\r\n    <li>They can automatically write code</li>\r\n    <li><strong>They standardize web development practices</strong></li>\r\n    <li>They eliminate the need for testing</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>19. What is the correct method in the History API to refresh the current webpage?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>history.update()</li>\r\n    <li><strong>history.go(0) or history.go()</strong></li>\r\n    <li>history.reloadCurrent()</li>\r\n    <li>history.reload()</li>\r\n    <li>history.refresh()</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>20. What is the function of Location.replace() method?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>It replaces the current URL with a new one without adding to history</strong></li>\r\n    <li>It updates the current URL's query string</li>\r\n    <li>It redirects to a default URL without reloading the page</li>\r\n    <li>It reloads the current URL</li>\r\n    <li>It adds a new URL to the history stack</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>21. What is the purpose of Location.reload() method?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>To reload the current URL</strong></li>\r\n    <li>To delete the current URL's history</li>\r\n    <li>To refresh the browser cache for the current URL</li>\r\n    <li>To save the current URL</li>\r\n    <li>To update the current URL's hash</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>22. What specific information does the Location.href property of a web page return?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>A random internet meme</li>\r\n    <li>The ID of the current element</li>\r\n    <li><strong>The current URL in its entirety</strong></li>\r\n    <li>The title of the current document</li>\r\n    <li>The protocol of the current URL</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>23. When was the term 'single-page application' first discussed?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>When dinosaurs roamed the internet</li>\r\n    <li>After a big party in Silicon Valley</li>\r\n    <li>During the year 2010</li>\r\n    <li><strong>As early as 2003</strong></li>\r\n    <li>In the year 2005</li>\r\n    <li>Sometime in the 1990s</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>24. Which event is associated with the History API for detecting when the active history entry changes?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>modifyHistory</li>\r\n    <li>historyHokeyPokey</li>\r\n    <li><strong>popstate</strong></li>\r\n    <li>historyShift</li>\r\n    <li>changeState</li>\r\n    <li>historyChange</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>25. Which History API property indicates the total number of entries in the browser's history stack?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>history.pages</li>\r\n    <li>history.size</li>\r\n    <li>history.total</li>\r\n    <li>history.count</li>\r\n    <li><strong>history.length</strong></li>\r\n    <li>history.stack</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>26. Which JavaScript framework is NOT typically associated with SPAs?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Meteor.js</li>\r\n    <li>React</li>\r\n    <li>Ember.js</li>\r\n    <li><strong>jQuery</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Vue.js</li>\r\n    <li>AngularJS</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>27. Which main feature does the History API offer access to?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>The browser's session cookies</li>\r\n    <li><strong>The user's personal browsing history</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Access to the browser's download history</li>\r\n    <li>A list of bookmarks in the browser</li>\r\n    <li>The browser's session history</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>28. Which method is used to move backward through the user's history?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>history.rewind()</li>\r\n    <li><strong>history.back()</strong></li>\r\n    <li>history.previous()</li>\r\n    <li>history.turnBackTime()</li>\r\n    <li>history.backward()</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>29. Which methods are part of the Location interface? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>reload()</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>toString()</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>replace()</strong></li>\r\n    <li>navigate()</li>\r\n    <li>open()</li>\r\n    <li><strong>assign()</strong></li>\r\n    <li>go()</li>\r\n    <li>singAlong()</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>30. Which methods are used to navigate the user's history in the History API? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>previous() and next()</li>\r\n    <li>reload() and refresh()</li>\r\n    <li>timeTravel() and freezeTime()</li>\r\n    <li>go() and stop()</li>\r\n    <li><strong>go() and go(-1)</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>back() and forward()</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>31. Which of these is a challenge associated with SPAs? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>Analytics</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Search engine optimization</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>Browser history management</strong></li>\r\n    <li>Mobile responsiveness</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Security scanning</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>32. Which properties can be found in the Location interface? (checkbox)</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li><strong>origin</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>search</strong></li>\r\n    <li>favoriteColor</li>\r\n    <li><strong>protocol</strong></li>\r\n    <li><strong>href</strong></li>\r\n    <li>length</li>\r\n    <li><strong>hash</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>33. Which property is used to get the protocol scheme of the URL?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>Location.urlProtocol</li>\r\n    <li>Location.pathname</li>\r\n    <li>Location.protocol</li>\r\n    <li>Location.host</li>\r\n    <li>Location.queryProtocol</li>\r\n    <li><strong>Location.origin</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n\r\n\r\n<article class=\"article\">\r\n  <h3>34. Which technology is crucial for real-time communication in SPAs?</h3>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>FTP</li>\r\n    <li>Morse code over telegraph lines</li>\r\n    <li>WebSockets</li>\r\n    <li>HTML</li>\r\n    <li>CSS</li>\r\n    <li><strong>GraphQL</strong></li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n</article>\r\n";
// Exports
/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = (code);

